er adding the final two corner\n  cases, `pytest -v cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py` also passed: 40 cocotb\n  pipeline tests, 0 failures.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=6 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  passed, 53 checks, 0 failures, first attempt; no counterexample or fix retry.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: passed, 5 ELFs; selftest and three random\n  programs each checked in both zero-wait and random-stall modes, plus canonical\n  stalled CoreMark CRC/completion validation.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench`: completed successfully with all three Gowin\n  placement options. Option 0: 72.717 MHz; option 1: 78.305 MHz; option 2:\n  78.305 MHz. Median: 78.305 MHz. Logic: 4,581; registers: 1,857; LUT-RAM: 32;\n  BSRAM: 5; DSP: 2. New reporting signals are absent from each synthesized\n  memory-output netlist, consistent with their verification-only role.\n- Canonical stalled CoreMark: 10 iterations in 4,197,447 marker-bracketed\n  cycles; all CRCs/completion/marker/bounds checks passed. These cycles equal\n  the supplied champion measurement. Fitness: 186.55 iterations/sec, about\n  3.96% below the supplied 194.25 champion and below the required 203.1855 gate.\n  This implementation is correct under the local gates but is not a demonstrated\n  champion replacement and does not meet the fitness acceptance threshold.\n\nNo architectural deviations from the hypothesis. The extra MEM availability\nguard is verification-only. Targeted instruction sequences remove false bubbles\nas intended, but the canonical stalled workload showed no bracketed-cycle\nreduction and median Fmax regressed. Evaluation-contract sources and nret=1\nare unchanged. Notes are kept under `cores/bench/` to honor the target-only\nedit scope.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
