{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_100","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Borrow-lookahead combinational divider\n\nReplaced only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU implementation in `rtl/alu.sv`\nwith one shared unsigned quotient/remainder network. Signed inputs are\nconverted to magnitudes; 32 constant-width rows process quotient bits\n31 down to 0 with 528 active subtraction bits in total. Each row uses\ntwo local prefix levels within four-bit groups and a balanced group\nprefix tree to derive both the final borrow and every difference bit.\nDivisor bits above the active row width reject subtraction, and low\nresidual bits pass through. Quotient/remainder selection precedes the\nshared signed correction. Explicit zero-divisor and INT_MIN/-1 overrides\npreserve RV32M results.\n\nThe real divider is excluded under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS; all eight ALTOPS\nformulas, multiplication, base integer operations, ports, pipeline,\nforwarding, memory handshakes, and retirement behavior remain unchanged.\nThe existing core declares nret=1; its contract was preserved.\n\nAdded a guarded include of core_pkg.sv in alu.sv because the exact\nrequested wildcard lint command otherwise encounters core.sv before its\ncompilation-unit type declarations. Existing source lists still work.\nNo other RTL file changed.\n\nRetained every existing test vector and added an integer-only,\ntruncation-toward-zero reference, checks of all four divide/remainder\noperations, observed quotient/remainder identities, power-of-two\nneighbors, equality/adjacency, sign combinations, INT_MIN/INT_MAX, zero\ndivisors, overflow, every quotient bit, every narrow-row divisor overflow\ncheck, alternating quotient bits, and deterministic uniform/biased random\noperands. Corrected obsolete test comments describing an iterative FSM.\n\nLocal validation so far:\n- Exact requested Verilator wildcard lint: PASS without warnings.\n- Verilator ALTOPS-mode lint: PASS without warnings.\n- pytest ALU runner: PASS (27 cocotb tests), 5.91 seconds.\n- NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench: PASS, two ELFs; selftest checked\n  against the ISS both unstalled and stalled, stalled CoreMark CRCs pass.\n- Formal gate: PASS, 53 passed / 0 failed, first attempt; no fixes.\n- Initial Gowin timing: option 0 4.506 MHz, 147 levels, 227.222 ns\n  worst arrival, 5,563 logic cells, 460 registers.\n- Initial three-option FPGA fitness: median 4.898 MHz, options\n  [4.506, 4.898, 4.898], unchanged 4,491,485 marker cycles, fitness\n  10.91 iterations/second (9.98 percent below the recorded baseline).\n\nThe initial explicit difference followed by a residual mux reduced area\nbut missed the performance target. Refined each row's selection to the\nequivalent expression x ^ ((y ^ borrow_in) & {N{subtract}}), which\ncombines difference/selection into one four-input Boolean function per\nbit while using exactly the same prefix borrow results. Lint passes;\nupdated arithmetic tests, cosim, and vendor timing are running.\n\nBaseline: median Fmax 5.442 MHz, 4,491,485 marker-bracketed cycles for\n10 iterations, fitness 12.12 iterations/second, 12,312 logic cells.\nThe required fitness improvement is greater than 4.6 percent.\n\nConcern: the divider still contains 32 dependent combinational rows;\nthe vendor flow must establish the timing benefit. Fast formal uses\nALTOPS and does not prove the real divider arithmetic; the ALU vectors\nand real-arithmetic cosim provide the local arithmetic checks.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
