{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git -C formal/riscv-formal status --short --untracked-files=no; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Shared RV32M multiplier implementation\n\nChanged only `rtl/alu.sv` and `test/test_alu.py` as implementation sources.\nThe ALU now dynamically sign-extends each operand to signed 33 bits and\ncomputes one combinational signed 66-bit product. MUL selects bits [31:0];\nMULH, MULHU and MULHSU share bits [63:32]. All real multiplier declarations\nand assignments are excluded from RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds. The four\nexisting ALTOPS expressions are unchanged. No ports, registers, instruction\nlatencies, divider logic, forwarding or retirement behavior changed.\n\nRetained every existing ALU vector and divider handshake assertion. Added\n76,864 exact Python-integer multiplication checks: the cross-product of\n96 boundary values for all four operations (36,864 results), plus 10,000\ndeterministic random operand pairs for all four operations (40,000 results).\nBoundary values include all requested constants and neighbors of powers\nof two. Random inputs include equal explicit coverage of the four sign\ncombinations. Operations change successively while operands remain fixed.\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- Verilator lint: pass with no warnings, both real arithmetic and ALTOPS.\n- ALU cocotb suite: all 30 tests pass, including the added checks.\n- `make bench`: canonical 2K, -O3, 10-iteration benchmark and all three\n  random retirement programs built from unchanged sources.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, five ELF programs tested;\n  selftest and random1/random2/random3 each checked with zero-wait buses\n  and with both instruction/data memory stalls.\n- Canonical stalled CoreMark: pass; ebreak reached, no out-of-bounds\n  access, both timing markers present and validation literal present.\n  CRCs: seed=e9f5, list=e714, matrix=1fd7, state=8e3a, final=fcaf.\n  Start marker cycle 15,150; stop marker cycle 4,212,597;\n  measured interval 4,197,447 cycles, unchanged from champion.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  pass on the first attempt, 53 checks passed and zero failed. The script\n  selected the unchanged nret=1 wrapper/config automatically. No formal\n  counterexamples, retries or RTL fixes were needed.\n- Complete `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` evaluator: pass.\n  All three placement options succeeded at 53.382, 53.083 and 53.083 MHz;\n  median Fmax is 53.083 MHz, versus champion 49.269 MHz (+7.74%).\n  Mapped resources: 3,205 logic cells (champion 3,280), 925 registers,\n  40 LUT-RAM, seven BSRAM, two DSP blocks (champion six).\n  The evaluator independently validated canonical CoreMark and measured\n  4,197,447 bracketed cycles for 10 iterations. Fitness is\n  53.083e6 * 10 / 4,197,447 = 126.46 iterations/second, versus 117.38\n  champion (+7.74%, exceeding the 4.6% threshold).\n\nNo architectural deviations from the hypothesis. NRET=1 is supplied to\nthe existing cosim build because its standalone default is NRET=2; the\ncore.yaml and all evaluation/contract sources remain unchanged.\nThe fast formal gate uses ALTOPS and does not prove the real multiplier;\nreal arithmetic is checked by the ALU suite and full retirement cosim.\nThe implementation reproduces the isolated prototype's mapped resources,\nall three Fmax measurements, cycle count and fitness. All requested local\ngates have completed successfully. No unresolved implementation concerns\nwere observed; full arithmetic SMT (`formal-deep`) was not run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
