.b(b), .busy(div_busy), .done(div_done), .result(div_result)\n   );\n \n-  // 64-bit products, computed once and selected per op.\n-  // mul_ss/mul_su low halves are unused (only MULH/MULHSU read the high\n-  // half). Verilator's UNUSEDSIGNAL is silenced locally — the unused\n-  // bits are dead-code-eliminated by Yosys.\n-  /* verilato\n…[8762 of 11834 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7f7a478d05d45ae4]…\ndrain)\n+    //   - m_wait      -> hold        (older MEM/WB instructions still drain)\n     //   - load_use    -> bubble      (1-cycle stall between LOAD + use)\n     //   - redirect    -> bubble      (kill wrong-path)\n     //   - otherwise   -> capture\n     // dmem_stall takes precedence over load_use's bubble: re-evaluate\n     // load_use next cycle when the bus unblocks. flush_id is 1 only when\n     // we want bubble (not hold).\n-    stall_id      = dmem_stall || load_use_hazard || div_wait;\n+    stall_id      = dmem_stall || load_use_hazard || m_wait;\n     // redirect is already qualified by EX acceptance. It must override\n     // raw wrong-path source-bit load-use interlocks at the ID register.\n-    flush_id      = redirect || (load_use_hazard && !dmem_stall && !div_wait);\n+    flush_id      = redirect || (load_use_hazard && !dmem_stall && !m_wait);\n     // EX/MEM register: holds on dmem_stall (LOAD waits in MEM until the\n     // bus delivers).\n     stall_ex_mem  = dmem_stall;\nMon Oct  5 01:13:22 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
