{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd={'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r10s0','title':'Select ADD operands after shared target arithmetic','category':'micro_opt','motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 bracketed cycles. A fresh unchanged Gowin placement-one run reproduces that Fmax and identifies alu_src and is_auipc as launches on the worst EX-to-ID paths. Current ALU ADD places both operand-selection muxes before its native adder. EX separately already computes pc+imm and rs1+imm for branch/JALR targets. No LESSONS.md exists. Previous address-only separation, registered one-hot ALU selection and trap-enable simplification failed to clear acceptance; this proposal targets the full ADD producer path without another register or operation-selector bank.''','hypothesis':'''Move ADD operand choice after native addition and explicitly share EX target adders with the ADD architectural-result path. Keep the current pipeline, instruction latency, bus handshakes, prediction policy and finalized EX > MEM > RF forwarding unchanged. This is one local arithmetic factoring optimization.\n\nIn EX compute three native full-width unsigned sums from existing ID/EX flops: rr=rs1_val+rs2_val, ri=rs1_val+imm, pi=pc+imm. The selected ADD result is is_auipc ? pi : alu_src ? ri : rr. Reuse pi as the existing direct branch/JAL target and ri as the existing JALR sum before bit-zero clearing. Do not instantiate another copy of these target expressions. All sums retain modulo-2\"'^32 carry behavior and full address width. Keep the native Gowin adders, avoiding carry-select expansion.\n\nGive alu a default-disabled PREPARED_ADD parameter and a prepared-add input. EX enables that parameter, and only the ALU_ADD case takes the prepared result. Standalone ALU users retain a+b with the default parameter. Keep the existing alu_a/alu_b routing for every other operation, all result-case selection, the shared formatted native multiplier and its launch boundary, the sticky iterative divider, and each exact ALTOPS formula. ALTOPS ADD must use the same correct selected result when enabled; its M-operation formulas are unchanged.\n\nThe intended gain is preventing alu_src/is_auipc transitions from traversing operand muxes and then a complete ADD carry chain before forwarding and the next ID capture. Existing target adders supply the immediate sums, so the implementation may also remove the mux-fed ADD network rather than pay for three new independent datapaths. Extra fanout, final selection and routing remain risks. An eight percent expected fitness gain has low confidence and is not a measured acceptance claim. At 4197447 cycles, median Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 85.286 MHz to beat 203.1855 iter/sec, the champion plus 4.6 percent.\n\nRetain exact nret=1 top-level IO, source-value capture and held operands, x0 and WB bypass, PC/link semantics, alignment and illegal traps, accepted EX predictor training and immediate recovery, strict retirement order, progress, once-only memory effects, bounds, true RV32IM/ALTOPS arithmetic, canonical CRCs, completion text and marker brackets. Change no evaluation-contract file. Use existing arithmetic, pipeline, decoder, formal and retirement-cosim gates, then score actual validated CoreMark throughput times fresh median Gowin Fmax.'\"''','expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},'changes':[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Factor the existing direct-target and JALR native sums into shared full-width pi and ri wires, add the raw-register rr sum, and select the prepared ADD result after arithmetic using existing registered controls. Enable the ALU prepared-add mode. Preserve all other datapaths, control timing, traps, recovery, producer qualifications, stall/divider protocols and RVFI payloads.'''},{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add a default-disabled PREPARED_ADD parameter and an input for the selected native ADD result. Only ALU_ADD changes under the enabled mode; retain original standalone behavior, all other cases and exact ALTOPS/M-extension arithmetic. Ensure strict real/ALTOPS lint and all existing source-list users remain valid.'''},{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Drive the new optional input for strict standalone lint and preserve every original real/ALTOPS assertion. Verify default-mode ADD still uses a/b independently of that input. Use integrated pipeline coverage to exercise prepared mode.'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve all original assertions and cover raw ADD, positive/negative ADDI, AUIPC with arbitrary encoded source fields, full-width overflow, load/store effective addresses and direct/JALR targets. Include immediate consumers through EX forwarding, youngest-writer priority, x0, stalled loads, division holds and recovery. Require exact RVFI operands/results/PC/trap/order and stable once-only memory handshakes. Run existing formal/cosim and unchanged canonical CoreMark validation before median vendor scoring.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised schema-valid hypothesis written')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
