{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_52", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261005-003-r7s2','hyp-20261005-002-r8s1']:\n  print(d['id']); print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261005-003-r7s2\nCompute the full 32-bit direct PC-relative destination in ID, in parallel with operand access, and register it at the existing ID/EX acceptance boundary as pc_relative_target = in.pc + decoded_imm. Add only that one word to id_ex_t. Retain the original PC and sign-extended immediate because other instruction paths and RVFI still use them. Do not add a pipeline stage or compute a predictor target-equality bit through the asynchronous BTB lookup in ID.\n\nIn EX replace its PC+immediate direct-target calculation with the accepted instruction's registered pc_relative_target. Use that destination for conditional branches and JAL, full-width saved-prediction target verification, predictor update_target even on a not-taken branch, and the corresponding architectural redirect destination. Keep JALR's full rs1+imm calculation and bit-zero clearing in EX, as it depends on finalized architectural operands. Keep PC+4 fallthrough and JAL/JALR link computation unchanged. The intended timing gain is removing the direct-target carry chain from EX's predictor verification/training/recovery cone; destination formation in ID runs independently of forwarded branch operands.\n\nPreserve exactly the current 64-entry direct-mapped BTB, full tags and absolute stored targets, two-bit saturating counters, unconditional-jump behavior, PC-only asynchronous lookup, reset-only validity, full range/alignment guards, weak replacement initialization and matching-only stale invalidation. Retain the balanced branch comparator, actual direction resolution, target mismatch 