{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_76", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r11s0',\n'title':'Give the native multiplier a dedicated operand launch bank',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion reaches 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 bracketed cycles. A fresh unchanged placement-option-one run reproduces 81.537 MHz. Its limiting paths terminate repeatedly at the multiplier DSP input register even for ALU/control and instruction-ready feedback. General finalized architectural operands currently also serve as multiplier inputs, allowing synthesis to absorb their launch registers into fixed-location DSP resources. Separating those physical storage roles can reduce routing constraints on the ordinary operand/branch network. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior prepared sign bits succeeded, while pipeline multiplication, ALU one-hot selection and prepared shift amounts failed to clear acceptance. This proposal preserves single-cycle multiplication.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one dedicated pair of signed 33-bit multiplier operand registers in ID, separate from the original ID/EX bundle. On reset clear these two registers. Otherwise capture them when \"'!stall and the unchanged decoder'\"'s ALU operation is any of MUL, MULH, MULHU or MULHSU. Capture the existing finalized EX > MEM > RF/WB-bypassed source values with exactly the current operation-dependent extension: A sign-extends only for MULH/MULHSU, B only for MULH. Both zero-extend for MUL and MULHU. Hold the pair on every nonmultiply decode and every genuine ID hold. The distinct multiply-only write enable prevents these hardware operand words from being merged with the general architectural source registers, which keep their original acceptance and bubble behavior.\n\nThe hardware-only bank may capture a discarded younger multiply on a recovery edge when \"'!stall, and may retain stale payload during bubbles. Do not qualify this payload capture with late redirect/flush or fetched-instruction validity. This introduces no instruction acceptance: the original ID/EX register still clears its entire bundle on reset, flush or an advancing invalid fetch, and its original valid/controls alone govern EX execution, forwarding, retirement, predictor updates and memory effects. An accepted valid multiply always captures its own finalized operands at the original ID/EX edge; EX/MEM uses the old bank value at that edge and the next instruction uses the new value afterward. A squashed bank value has no effect and is replaced before any later accepted multiply executes. Preserve complete original ID/EX zero bubbles and all existing assertions; do not weaken them to permit speculative architectural payload.\n\nExport the bank to EX through dedicated signed [32:0] internal ports and wire it straight to the existing alu.mul_a/mul_b inputs. Keep mul_product = mul_a * mul_b, the shared native 33-by-33 multiplication and two-DSP intent, low/high result selection, original stage boundaries, one multiply per cycle, instruction latency and youngest-writer forwarding unchanged. EX must not place an opcode, operand-source or validity mux between the dedicated bank and those ALU ports. Keep the original architectural rs1_val/rs2_val and extension fields and their accepted values/clearing/holds intact; old extension fields become unused by real multiplier wiring and may be annotated for strict lint, without changing test monitors. ALTOPS multiplication still uses original architectural ALU operands and exact existing formulas; the hardware bank must not change formal substitutes.\n\nPreserve existing true and ALTOPS arithmetic, divider launch/sticky completion/consume, branch comparator/prediction/recovery/training, decoder defaults and legality, traps and link/address semantics, all memory handshakes and lanes, nret=1 and exact top-level IO/RVFI, consecutive order, progress, memory bounds, canonical CRCs, completion text and timing markers. Add no execution stage, multiplier FSM, scheduling bubble, predictor delay, RAM or evaluation-contract change. The optimization is physically separating multiplier launch storage from general operand storage at an existing boundary.\n\nPredict six percent fitness improvement with low confidence pending the final isolated prototype measurements. Extra storage and decoded multiply-enable fanout may offset improved routing, and residual EX/predictor/ID paths may remain limiting. Do not claim a demonstrated win from this estimate. Expect identical canonical CoreMark cycle count, but score actual bracketed cycles and all three fresh Gowin placement options. Acceptance requires fitness above 203.1855 iter/sec, roughly 85.286 MHz at 4197447 cycles. Run unchanged correctness gates; all hardware multiply variants must remain exact, including dependent multiply chains and signed high halves.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Add a separate hardware-only signed 33-bit operand register pair and output ports. Reset clears it; \"'!stall and any validated decoded multiply op captures exact finalized, correctly extended sources; other cycles hold it. Keep flush/valid out of this pair'\"'s enable. Preserve the entire original ID/EX bundle capture/reset/flush/hold protocol and all architectural operand/extension fields.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Add the two dedicated internal operand inputs and connect them directly to the unchanged ALU native multiplier inputs. Preserve arithmetic and ALTOPS operand routing, all producer/acceptance/hold/recovery behavior, latency and EX/MEM metadata. Annotate only genuinely unused original multiplier extension fields for warning-clean lint in real/ALTOPS modes.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire the dedicated operand pair from ID to EX, retaining original interstage bundles, forwarding, hazard controls, top-level IO and nret=1 RVFI. Introduce no multiplier wait or issue restriction.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every current architectural and whole-bundle-zero assertion. Add bank-capture and retention checks with all four multiply variants, independent consecutive multiplies, dependency chains, competing EX/MEM/WB writers, x0, load/division operands and immediate consumers. Cover wrong-path multiply capture on redirect, bubbles and nonmultiply gaps, imem/dmem holds, reset and backpressure across result transfer. Require exact signed extension, raw RVFI sources/results/order, unchanged latency, stable held operands and once-only side effects. Run unchanged real/ALTOPS arithmetic tests, strict lint, formal, retirement cosim and canonical stalled CoreMark/vendor fitness; do not weaken any gate.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final single-angle hypothesis written and schema validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
