{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,160p' CLAUDE.md\nls -la /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-nolessons-rep2/cores/bench\nls -la /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-nolessons-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees\"", "aggregated_output": "# CLAUDE.md — non-negotiable invariants and don't-touch list\n\nEvery item below was a real bug in the prior Chisel iteration. Each must be\nenforced by a check that fails loudly when violated. **Do not weaken these\nchecks** to make a hypothesis pass.\n\n## Hard invariants\n\n| # | Invariant                                                                                                  | Enforced by                                  |\n|---|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|\n| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\n| 2 | `rvfi_trap = 1` iff the retiring instruction is illegal per RV32IM (decoder default = illegal)             | `riscv-formal ill` check                     |\n| 3 | EBREAK is the *only* SYSTEM (opcode `0x73`) instruction the core treats as valid; ECALL / CSR / MRET trap  | dedicated decoder unit tests                 |\n| 4 | `rvfi_order` strictly monotonic +1 per retirement across both channels combined (no gaps, no duplicates). When both channels retire in the same cycle, channel-0 order = N and channel-1 order = N+1.                                       | `riscv-formal unique` check                  |\n| 5 | CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic instruction stream                                           | `riscv-formal liveness` check                |\n| 5b | M-extension arithmetic produces RV32M-correct bit results    \n…[8026 of 11098 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:da5ec60ad826f0df]…\n` (formal without ALTOPS — slow but the only path\n     that proves real arithmetic via SMT). Run periodically, not in\ntotal 68\ndrwxrwx---+ 8 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 02:05 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 02:03 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup    0 Oct  5 02:03 CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  545 Oct  5 05:39 core.yaml\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 02:39 experiments\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 02:04 generated\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 02:03 obj_dir\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 05:39 rtl\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 05:39 test\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 09:35 worktrees\ntotal 40\ndrwxrwx---+  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 09:35 .\ndrwxrwx---+  8 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 02:05 ..\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 09:39 hyp-20261005-001-r13s0-hypgen\ndrwxrwx---+  9 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 09:38 hyp-20261005-002-r13s1-hypgen\ndrwxrwx---+  9 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct  5 09:39 hyp-20261005-003-r13s2-hypgen\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The schema-valid hypothesis file is written. It proposes balanced group carry selection for the existing EX sums, with an estimated 8% gain and low confidence. I’ll use the remaining time to test an isolated RTL prototype and check whether Gowin timing supports that estimate."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_20", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nbase=Path('cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype')\nrtl=base/'rtl'\nrtl.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nfor p in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'):\n shutil.copy2(p,rtl/p.name)\nhelper='''// Exact 32-bit group carry-select addition.\nmodule fast_add32 (\n  input wire [31:0] a, b,\n  input wire carry_in,\n  output wire [31:0] sum\n);\n  wire [3:0] sum_zero [0:7];\n  wire [3:0] sum_one [0:7];\n  wire [7:0] group_g [0:3];\n  wire [7:0] group_p [0:3];\n  wire [7:0] carry;\n  for (genvar k=0; k<8; k++) begin : g_leaf\n    wire [4:0] zero_ext;\n    assign zero_ext = {1'b0,a[4*k +: 4]} + {1'b0,b[4*k +: 4]};\n    assign sum_zero[k] = zero_ext[3:0];\n    assign sum_one[k] = a[4*k +: 4] + b[4*k +: 4] + 4'd1;\n    assign group_g[0][k] = zero_ext[4];\n    assign group_p[0][k] = &(a[4*k +: 4] \"'^ b[4*k +: 4]);\n    if (k==0) assign carry[k] = carry_in;\n    else assign carry[k] = group_g[3][k-1] | (group_p[3][k-1] & carry_in);\n    assign sum[4*k +: 4] = carry[k] ? sum_one[k] : sum_zero[k];\n  end\n  for (genvar level=0; level<3; level++) begin : g_level\n    for (genvar k=0; k<8; k++) begin : g_prefix\n      if (k >= (1<<level)) begin\n        assign group_g[level+1][k] = group_g[level][k]\n          | (group_p[level][k] & group_g[level][k-(1<<level)]);\n        assign group_p[level+1][k] = group_p[level][k] & group_p[level][k-(1<<level)];\n      end else begin\n        assign group_g[level+1][k] = group_g[level][k];\n        assign group_p[level+1][k] = group_p[level][k];\n      end\n    end\n  end\nendmodule\n'\"'''\n(rtl/'fast_add32.sv').write_text(helper)\np=rtl/'alu.sv'\ns=p.read_text().replace('  always_comb begin\\\\n    shamt', '''  wire [31:0] add_result, sub_result;\n  fast_add32 u_add(.a(a), .b(b), .carry_in(1'b0), .sum(add_result));\n  fast_add32 u_sub(.a(a), .b(~b), .carry_in(1'b1), .sum(sub_result));\n\n  always_comb begin\n    shamt''').replace('ALU_ADD:    out = a + b;','ALU_ADD:    out = add_result;').replace('ALU_SUB:    out = a - b;','ALU_SUB:    out = sub_result;')\np.write_text(s)\np=rtl/'ex_stage.sv';s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('  always_comb begin\\\\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)', '''  wire [31:0] pc_relative_sum;\n  fast_add32 u_pc_target(.a(in.pc), .b(in.imm), .carry_in(1'b0), .sum(pc_relative_sum));\n  fast_add32 u_jalr_target(.a(rs1), .b(in.imm), .carry_in(1'b0), .sum(jalr_sum));\n\n  always_comb begin\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)''').replace('branch_target = in.pc + in.imm;','branch_target = pc_relative_sum;').replace('    jalr_sum    = rs1 + in.imm;\\\\n','').replace(': (in.pc + in.imm);',': pc_relative_sum;')\np.write_text(s)\n(base/'miter.sv').write_text('''module miter(input [31:0] a,b,input carry_in,output ok);\n  wire [31:0] sum;\n  fast_add32 dut(a,b,carry_in,sum);\n  assign ok = sum == (a + b + {31'b0,carry_in});\nendmodule\n''')\nprint('Isolated prototype:',rtl)\nPY\nverilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/core_pkg.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/alu.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/branch_predictor.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/core.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/decoder.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/divider.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/ex_stage.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/fast_add32.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/forward_unit.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/hazard_unit.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/id_stage.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/if_stage.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/imm_gen.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/mem_stage.sv cores/bench/generated/hyp13_add_prototype/rtl/reg_file.sv co