{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r13s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261005-001-r13s0\ntitle: \\\"Prepare base ALU operands before the execute launch boundary\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 timed\n  CoreMark cycles. Long paths repeatedly cross EX's AUIPC/source-immediate\n  operand selection, ALU result generation and forwarding before ID\n  captures the next operands. Preparing multiplier signedness before\n  ID/EX previously raised fitness from 170.74 to 184.91; the ordinary\n  ALU still has two operand-selection muxes after that launch boundary.\n  LESSONS.md is absent. The micro_opt history was reviewed: one-hot\n  result selection, prepared shift control, dedicated multiplier launch\n  and raw fetch-address routing all regressed. A local prototype with\n  grouped carry-select adders also regressed to 66.725 MHz. Preserve\n  native arithmetic and move its input selection to the existing ID\n  acceptance edge instead of changing the carry or pipeline topology.\nhypothesis: |\n  Preselect the two ordinary ALU operands in ID and register them at\n  the existing ID/EX boundary. Add exactly two 32-bit fields, alu_a and\n  alu_b, to id_ex_t. Capture alu_a = dec_is_auipc ? in.pc : rs1_final\n  and alu_b = dec_alu_src ? imm : rs2_final on precisely the same edge\n  that currently captures finalized rs1_val/rs2_val, immediate, control\n  and prediction metadata. In EX drive the ordinary ALU a/b inputs\n  directly from these prepared fields, eliminating the PC-versus-rs1\n  and immediate-versus-rs2 data muxes after the execute launch flops.\n  This is one operand-preparation micro-optimization with unchanged\n  stages, instruction latency, acceptance and interlock behavior.\n\n  Keep the complete existing raw rs1_val/rs2_val and PC/immediate fields.\n  They continue feeding branch comparisons, JALR targets, stores, RVFI\n  and the multiplier's formatted raw operands. Keep multiplier sign\n  preparation and its direct raw-operand launch exactly as written.\n  Do not route multiplication through the prepared ALU operands or\n  introduce a duplicate multiplier bank. Base arithmetic, shifts and\n  comparisons use the prepared values. The shared divider and every\n  ALTOPS expression receive the exact same selected values as before,\n  including capturing a request once and preserving sticky completion.\n  Leave alu.sv and its native arithmetic/result selection unchanged.\n\n  Retain ID's current reset/flush/invalid-bubble assignment of the entire\n  register to zero. It must clear the two new fields as well. A genuine\n  ID hold retains all raw and prepared operands together, even as older\n  MEM/WB producers drain; never refresh them during dmem or division\n  stalls. Use the existing finalized forwarding results and decoded\n  controls without weakening x0 handling, producer qualification or\n  EX > MEM > RF priority. The normal capture arm is the only place that\n  selects and records new ALU inputs. Preserve encoded unused-source\n  RVFI behavior and conservative load-use detection.\n\n  Preserve PC+4 and control-flow target arithmetic, the balanced branch\n  comparator, full-width target/range/alignment checks, branch and jump\n  traps, links, immediate accepted recovery and once-only predictor\n  training. Leave fetch masking, predictor lookup/storage/policy and\n  memory bus outputs/handshakes unchanged. Do not move forwarding to EX,\n  alter RF storage, add a decode stage or speculate operand captures.\n\n  The intended gain is removing selection depth between the execute\n  launch registers and native ALU operations, especially the AUIPC and\n  immediate arithmetic feedback paths. ID already resolves the operands;\n  its prepared muxes run before those launch flops. The two new words\n  cost up to 64 registers, and added ID muxing or routing may erase the\n  benefit. Estimate six percent fitness improvement with low confidence\n  pending vendor timing. Expect unchanged canonical CoreMark cycles,\n  but score actual marker-bracketed iterations/cycle times median Gowin\n  Fmax. Acceptance requires fitness above 203.1855 iter/sec, approximately\n  85.286 MHz at 4197447 cycles.\n\n  Validate register/immediate and AUIPC selection using independent\n  architectural results, with dependency chains and both bus stalls.\n  Run strict lint in real and ALTOPS modes, existing arithmetic/decoder/\n  pipeline suites, unchanged single-channel formal and retirement cosim,\n  canonical stalled CoreMark and median vendor timing. Preserve nret=1\n  and exact external IO, every hard invariant, full-width modular results,\n  strict retirement order, default-illegal decoding, traps, progress,\n  held operands, memory bounds, canonical CRCs, completion text and\n  timing markers. Only listed RTL and cocotb tests may change.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add 32-bit alu_a and alu_b prepared operand fields to id_ex_t.\n      Preserve raw source values, PC/immediate, multiplier sign fields,\n      every existing control and the other pipeline bundle definitions.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      In the existing accepted capture arm register AUIPC-selected\n      alu_a and immediate-selected alu_b from finalized ID operands.\n      Preserve the complete reset/flush/bubble clear and genuine hold\n      protocol, all forwarding, x0, decoder and multiplier sign logic.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive ordinary ALU operands directly from the two prepared fields\n      instead of selecting PC/rs1 and immediate/rs2 in EX. Preserve raw\n      operand use for branches, JALR, stores, multiplier formatting and\n      RVFI; retain every acceptance, trap, predictor and division signal.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all existing assertions and add independent arithmetic\n      checks for register/immediate operations, LUI/AUIPC, zero sources,\n      load-forwarded operands, overlapping writers and dependency chains.\n      Exercise load-use, imem/dmem stalls, DIV/REM holds and recovery.\n      Check exact RVFI sources/results/PCs/order, once-only memory effects\n      and that raw and prepared operands stay aligned through every hold.\n''')\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated hypothesis is schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
