5 iter/sec, approximately 85.286 MHz at 4197447 cycles.\n\nProve the combinational unsigned and signed results equivalent to full-width reference comparisons for arbitrary operands. Retain all existing tests and extend arithmetic tests with each significance boundary, competing high/low group decisions, equal operands, signed extremes and deterministic random inputs. Run real and ALTOPS strict lint, existing decoder/arithmetic/pipeline suites, unchanged single-channel formal and retirement cosim, canonical stalled CoreMark and median Gowin timing. Preserve nret=1, exact external IO, default-illegal decoding, all traps, precise RVFI sources/results/PCs, strict retirement order, progress, memory bounds, canonical CRCs, completion text and MMIO brackets. Only the listed RTL and cocotb test may change.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add one shared eight-leaf balanced four-bit magnitude comparator over existing a/b inputs. Derive signed less-than from operand signs and the unsigned root. Replace only ALU_SLT/ALU_SLTU result expressions. Preserve ports, operand/result selection, all other real/base operations and every M-extension ALTOPS formula. Use constant-index logic and keep the EX branch comparator unchanged.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain all arithmetic and latency assertions. Extend SLT/SLTU checks with independent signed/unsigned integer reference comparisons for equality, every four-bit significance boundary, conflicting significant versus lower groups, all sign combinations, INT_MIN/INT_MAX and seeded random operands. Include selected-immediate comparison coverage through unchanged pipeline tests and run existing lint/formal/cosim and canonical vendor fitness gates.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Balanced ALU comparison h