{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_32", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x['id']=='hyp-20261005-002-r12s1': print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Restructure the two register-file read ports as unified architectural\noperand networks containing the stored register words and three virtual\nproducer banks: current EX result, current MEM result and current WB\nresult. Each port computes mutually exclusive producer masks with\nyoungest-writer priority EX > MEM > WB > stored RF. Integrate those\nproducer terms into a balanced masked-OR reduction instead of first\nselecting WB versus RF inside reg_file and then EX/MEM versus that\nresult inside id_stage. ID receives already finalized operands and\ncaptures them in the existing ID/EX flops. This is one structural change\nto the register-read/bypass topology, with no added instruction stage.\n\nKeep the current 31 resettable constant-index flop words and balanced\nstored-word read trees. For each source address s compute ex_hit from\neffective ex_en, nonzero ex_rd and ex_rd==s; similarly mem_hit and\nwb_hit. Form ex_select=ex_hit, mem_select=!ex_hit && mem_hit,\nwb_select=!ex_hit && !mem_hit && wb_hit, and\nrf_select=!ex_hit && !mem_hit && !wb_hit. The final word is the OR of\nthe four separately masked data sources, using a balanced reduction.\nDo not turn this back into nested data ternaries. Producer hits exclude\nx0 and the stored x0 leaf remains zero, so x0 requires no final wide\ndata mux. Preserve raw encoded source-address handling, including unused\nfields, so every existing RVFI source-value comparison remains valid.\n\nDrive EX and MEM banks from exactly the existing producer_w_en and\nproducer_data signals and existing destination tags. Their qualification\nalready excludes bubbles, unavailable loads/divisions, nonwrites, x0\nand effective trapping writes. Do not simplify or weaken those guards.\nWB retains its current write-first semantics and existing write enable.\nSynchronous storage writes remain WB-only; virtual producer banks are\nread routing, never additional architectural writes. Both read ports\nindependently choose their youngest matching writer, including all\ncombinations of same-rd EX/MEM/WB producers.\n\nRemove the separate core forwarding-unit instance and ID's forwarding\ndata muxes; leave the unused standalone module available if tests need\nit. Connect producer tags/data/enables directly to reg_file. ID still\ncaptures raw finalized rs1/rs2, prepares multiplier sign bits on that\nsame acceptance edge, and holds every operand through genuine stalls.\nExecute continues launching from these flops, with no late bypass,\nsynchronous RF read, speculative operand update or pipeline change.\n\nPreserve load-use interlocking, both bus handshakes, accepted immediate\nEX recovery, predictor lookup/training, trap suppression, divider\nlaunch/sticky completion/consume, older WB draining and all true/ALTOPS\narithmetic. No new producer may bypass an unavailable result. Reset and\nflush behavior remain the existing protocol; architectural source\ncapture happens only on accepted ID transactions.\n\nPredict six percent fitness improvement with low confidence pending\nvendor timing. The intended gain is fewer cascaded operand-selection\nlevels and less duplicated bypass routing, with unchanged CoreMark\ninstruction scheduling and expected bracket cycles. Remaining branch\nqualification and predictor feedback may still dominate. Do not claim\nacceptance from an RTL depth estimate: compare actual canonical stalled\nCoreMark iterations/cycle times median Gowin Fmax. Fitness must exceed\n203.1855 iter/sec; at 4197447 cycles this requires about 85.29 MHz.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and exact top-level memory/channel-0 RVFI IO, strict\nretirement order, default-illegal decoding and traps, bounded progress,\nmemory bounds, canonical CRCs, completion text and timing markers.\nRun unchanged lint, decoder/arithmetic tests, single-channel formal,\nretirement cosim and final vendor/CoreMark scoring. Only allowed RTL\nand cocotb tests may change. Do not alter wrappers, check settings,\nevaluators, benchmarks, contract files or core.yaml.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
