{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x['id']=='hyp-20261005-002-r7s1':print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x['id']=='hyp-20261005-002-r7s1':print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Change only the register-file storage topology: replace the 31 large\nresettable flop words with four independent eight-row asynchronous\ndistributed-memory banks, replicated once for each read port. Bank\nindex is address[4:3], local row is address[2:0]. Each bank owns two\nunreset logic [31:0] arrays [0:7], one for rs1 and one for rs2, with\nasynchronous indexed reads and identical synchronous writes. Read\nevery bank's selected local row, then select the addressed bank with\na shallow four-input mux. Use portable inferred memories, not vendor\nprimitives, and never introduce a synchronous read or another stage.\n\nEach bank's write enable is !reset && w_en && w_addr != 0 and a sized\nequality between w_addr[4:3] and its constant bank number. Both copies\nreceive w_data at w_addr[2:0] on the same edge. Arrays have no reset,\ninitialization loop or per-row constant-index flop coding. Maintain\na separate 32-bit written/valid bitmap: synchronous reset clears it,\na nonzero accepted write sets the corresponding bit, and bit zero\nremains clear. Reads of unwritten registers return zero, preserving\nthe current reset-clears-all observable behavior even across repeated\nresets with populated memories. Reset inhibits both payload writes\nand validity updates. Invalid raw memory bits must never affect a\nread result, execution, memory side effect or valid RVFI transaction.\n\nPreserve the current combinational read contract and priority exactly:\naddress zero returns zero; otherwise matching w_en/w_addr returns\nw_data in the same cycle; otherwise a written address returns the\nselected asynchronous bank word; otherwise return zero. Write-first\nbypass applies to both ports, including simultaneous collisions.\nKeep its current behavior during an asserted reset before the reset\nedge; synchronous reset wins over committing a pending write.\n\nThe essential structural condition is that shallow payload memories\nmap to distributed LUT RAM with asynchronous outputs. Gowin must not\nmap these arrays into synchronous BSRAM or absorb the existing ID/EX\noper\n…[2670 of 5742 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:014887fdd0492f6a]…\n not a\ndemonstrated champion replacement. At unchanged cycles, median Fmax\nmust exceed about 85.29 MHz and fitness must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec\nto clear that gate. Smaller gains must not be accepted as a win.\n\nThe four-bank storage topology is the strongest isolated structural\noption found in this investigation. Two sixteen-row banks, eight\nfour-row banks, alternate bank indexing and folding validity/write\nbypass into masked bank terms all timed worse. Moving RF commit earlier or preparing general ALU\noperands earlier also timed worse. Retain the specified four-bank\nasynchronous layout rather than combining those unsuccessful changes.\nExtra read replication, bank-output muxes, valid-bit qualification,\nthe remaining EX-to-ID path and the unfinished register-state proof\nare the practical limits. Final implementation must complete every\nunchanged correctness gate and obtain fresh median vendor timing and\ncanonical stalled marker-bracketed throughput. A timing or area gain\nwithout those checks is insufficient.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
