{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"agent_message","text":"None of the completed timing probes clears the acceptance threshold. I’m narrowing the proposal to source-aware load interlocks: immediate instructions currently stall when immediate bits resemble an rs2 dependency. The change also needs to preserve the existing RVFI values for unused encoded source fields; that path is now being checked."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_70", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Suppress false load-use bubbles with source-aware interlocks',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iterations/sec at 81.537 MHz with 4,197,447\nmarker-bracketed stalled CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The\nmicro_opt history shows that additional operand preparation, ALU\npredecode, raw fetch reads and relocated WB selection failed to clear\nthe 4.6 percent gate. Fresh isolated probes of factored RF reads,\nredundant x0 mux removal, ALU carry selection, shared shifts, one-hot\nforwarding and moved ADD selection also regressed; the unchanged\nchampion reproduced 81.537 MHz. A different local opportunity is that\nload-use detection compares both encoded source fields for every\ninstruction, including immediate bits that do not name an operand.\nThese false dependencies waste issue cycles and feed front-end holds.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Make the existing one-cycle load-use interlock aware of which encoded\nsource fields an instruction actually consumes. Keep the current\nsingle-issue pipeline, instruction acceptance boundaries, execution\nunits, forwarding priority, predictor and all bus-handshake protocols.\nThis is one local hazard predicate optimization, with no additional\ninstruction queue, stage, cache or execution mode.\n\nClassify source use from the original masked IF instruction opcode:\nrs1 is used by OP (0x33), OP-IMM (0x13), LOAD (0x03), STORE (0x23),\nBRANCH (0x63) and JALR (0x67); rs2 is used only by OP, STORE and\nBRANCH. All other opcodes use neither field. Conservatively retain\nthese uses for reserved funct encodings within those opcode classes;\nsource-use classification must not alter validated decoder legality.\nDefine load_use = existing_EX_load && rd_nonzero &&\n((uses_rs1 && rd_equals_rs1) || (uses_rs2 && rd_equals_rs2)).\nKeep the existing masked source addresses and readiness behavior.\nA matching immediate pseudo-rs2, LUI/AUIPC/JAL source field or\nunused SYSTEM/FENCE field must no longer insert a scheduling bubble.\nTrue dependencies, including store data and JALR bases, still interlock.\n\nPreserve the project's existing RVFI reporting of both raw encoded\nsource addresses and their architectural values, even for unused\nfields. Removing false bubbles must not leave a stale unused-source\nvalue in the retirement trace. Add a verification-only MEM producer\nconnection into EX. When an encoded source is unused, its address\nmatches the current effective nonzero MEM writer, and that writer is\navailable, use MEM producer_data solely for the corresponding\nEX/MEM rs1_val or rs2_val reporting field. Otherwise use the original\ncaptured value. Recompute the same conservative use classification\nfrom the saved instruction for this reporting correction. Both used\nsource values remain exactly the original finalized ID/EX operands.\n\nThese reporting muxes must never feed ALU/multiplier/divider operands,\nbranch comparisons, addresses, store data, producer forwarding or any\nacceptance control. They are pruned from the timed memory-output\nnetlist. Preserve source addresses, x0, youngest-writer priority and\nall existing RVFI assertions. The original effective MEM producer\nguards exclude bubbles, x0 and trapping/nonwriting instructions.\nDuring a genuine dmem hold EX cannot accept; the reporting value is\ncaptured only when the older memory instruction and younger EX\ninstruction can advance. Do not refresh or modify held ID/EX fields.\n\nKeep all existing load-use bubble, dmem/divider hold, imem masking,\nredirect-over-stall priority, EX acceptance, WB draining, once-only\nmemory effects and retirement order rules. Preserve nret=1 and exact\nexternal memory/RVFI IO, decoder default illegality and validated\nfunct checks, all traps, native RV32M and exact ALTOPS formulas,\nforward progress, full-width memory bounds, canonical CRCs, completion\ntext and start/stop markers. Do not modify any evaluation contract.\n\nPredict six percent fitness gain with low confidence from avoiding\nfalse issue bubbles and removing unused comparisons from hold control.\nThis estimate is not a demonstrated champion replacement. Added opcode\nclassification can hurt Fmax, and the fraction of false bubbles may be\nsmall. Measure actual canonical stalled marker cycles and all three\nGowin placement options; acceptance requires fitness above 203.1855\niterations/sec, not merely fewer cycles or a single timing probe.\nRun unchanged unit, formal and full-retirement cosim gates, including\nexact unused-source RVFI checks, before scoring the candidate.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'''Add source-use qualifiers to the existing two destination/source\ncomparisons. Preserve nonzero destination and EX load guards, masked\nfetch addresses, all hold/flush priorities and true dependency latency.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Derive the conservative opcode source-use qualifiers from if_id_w.instr\nand connect them to the interlock. Connect the existing effective MEM\nproducer tag/enable/data to EX only for unused-source RVFI correction.\nKeep top-level IO, memory routing and all original producer guards.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Correct only unused encoded source reporting fields at EX/MEM capture\nusing an available matching effective MEM producer. Classify from the\nsaved instruction, retain original used operands and every execute,\ntrap, redirect, training, bubble, hold and acceptance rule. Keep the\nnew connections out of all timed architectural datapaths.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all assertions. Add adjacent loads followed by ADDI/shift/load\nimmediates whose encoded rs2 matches the load destination, and by\nLUI/AUIPC/JAL/FENCE/SYSTEM with unused matching fields. Verify removal\nof exactly false bubbles, exact used and unused RVFI source values,\ntrue dependencies for both OP inputs, store data and JALR bases, x0,\nreserved encodings, youngest writers, imem/dmem stalls, misaligned\nloads, reset/recovery, order and once-only effects. Update only explicit\ncycle expectations for intentionally removed false hazards.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Written and schema validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
