{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_70", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r15s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-001-r15s0\ntitle: \"Four-bit carry lookahead for execute-stage sums\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion reaches 194.25 iterations/sec at 81.537 MHz, with 4197447\n  marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its recent timing paths repeatedly\n  cross EX arithmetic and ID operand capture or predictor maintenance.\n  A balanced four-bit branch comparator produced the last accepted gain;\n  fetch queues, predictor storage changes, source-aware hazards and unified\n  bypass routing subsequently failed to clear the acceptance margin.\n  LESSONS.md is absent. The micro_opt history includes failed combinational\n  divider lookahead but no grouped carry acceleration of ordinary execute\n  addition. That divider attempt repeated many dependent subtractors;\n  this proposal addresses a single 32-bit addition per feedback path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the native full-width addition/subtraction expressions on the\n  execute feedback paths with one reusable combinational 32-bit adder\n  built from eight four-bit groups and balanced group carry lookahead.\n  Apply the same arithmetic topology to ALU ADD/SUB and EX's PC+immediate,\n  rs1+immediate and PC+4 sums. This is one local carry-network optimization:\n  retain every register boundary, instruction latency and scheduling rule.\n  Do not change the fetch incrementer, divider or multiplier.\n\n  For operands x,y and carry-in cin, each group forms bit propagate\n  p=x XOR y and generate g=x AND y. Compute group propagate as the AND\n  of its four p bits and group generate as g3 OR p3*g2 OR p3*p2*g1 OR\n  p3*p2*p1*g0. Combine adjacent group (G,P) pairs in a constant-index\n  balanced prefix tree: G=G_high OR P_high*G_low, P=P_high*P_low.\n  Obtain each group's input carry from the prefix of all lower groups\n  and cin, avoiding a serial chain of eight group carry equations.\n  Within each group use a four-bit native addition with its calculated\n  carry-in, or equivalent explicitly expanded local carry equations.\n  No 32-bit native addition may remain behind this helper, since tha\n…[3114 of 6186 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f55eb10138fe8823]…\n identical sum between its existing consumers.\n      Preserve full-width targets, post-sum JALR bit-zero clearing, link\n      values, traps, branch comparison, producer guards, prediction\n      verification and all EX/MEM acceptance/reset/hold/bubble behavior.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all arithmetic assertions; add ADD/SUB boundary and seeded\n      random checks stressing carry/borrow across every four-bit boundary,\n      zero/all-ones operands and signed overflow with modulo-32 results.\n      Check the helper equivalently for unrestricted carry-in if directly\n      instantiated. Preserve all multiplier/divider real-result tests.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all architectural assertions and check carry-boundary ADDI,\n      AUIPC, address and JAL/JALR/branch target/link cases under instruction\n      and data stalls. Verify exact RVFI values, misalignment suppression,\n      redirect priority, held operands, order and once-only memory effects.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
