all is needed. Reset\n  clears pending validity and all table-valid bits, cancels queued work,\n  and dominates both capture and commit. Invalid pending slots do nothing.\n\n  Preserve allocation, weak initialization, saturating conditional updates,\n  jump-to-branch replacement, t\n…[1675 of 4747 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b86d8aeaf0e28c15]…\n bypass\n      live or pending updates to asynchronous lookup.\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all predictor policy assertions and adapt update observation\n      to the documented extra training edge. Check old lookup contents\n      before commit, consecutive same-row saturating updates, ordered\n      conflicting-tag replacement/invalidation, disabled updates, reset\n      with work pending and simultaneous commit/capture/lookup. Require\n      exactly one ordered commit per accepted transaction.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise back-to-back control-flow training and stale-target recovery\n      while imem/dmem readiness, load-use and division holds interrupt\n      execution. Keep exact retirement order, source/results, resolved PCs,\n      trap and wrong-path-store checks. Run existing formal/cosim and the\n      canonical stalled CoreMark validation; compare median vendor timing\n      and bracket cycles against the 126.46 iter/sec champion.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
