{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r.get('category')=='micro_opt' and 'r1s0' not in r['id'] and 'baseline' not in r['id']:\n  print(r['id'],r['title'])\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('Implementation notes:',r.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r.get('category')=='micro_opt' and 'r1s0' not in r['id'] and 'baseline' not in r['id']:\n  print(r['id'],r['title'])\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('Implementation notes:',r.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261005-001-r2s0 Remove redirect-driven instruction masking from the ID critical path\nMake one local optimization to branch-recovery timing: separate bubble\ncontrol from the instruction and ID/EX payload datapaths. Preserve the\nexisting pipeline registers, cycle latency, EX branch resolution, and\nsingle-channel retirement contract. Always expose raw imem_data as the\ncombinational IF instruction; express redirect or an unavailable fetch\nthrough out.valid rather than a 32-bit instruction-to-NOP mux. Decoding,\nregister-file addresses, and load-use comparisons must consequently have\nno combinational dependency on redirect.\n\nIn ID, split updates of payload fields from valid/control updates.\nReset still initializes the complete register. Outside reset, update\nPC, operands, immediate, destination/source addresses, and instruction\nwhenever the existing stall input is low, even if a flush or invalid\nfetch will make that captured payload a bubble. Do not put flush or\nin.valid in this payload write-enable or select a zero payload on flush.\nGive flush priority over stall only for valid and ctrl: flush makes\nvalid zero and ctrl zero; otherwise a held stage retains both, and an\nadvancing stage captures in.valid and either the validated decoded\ncontrol for a valid instruction or zero control for an invalid fetch.\nThus arbitrary wrong-path payload bits are harmless while every bubble\nhas mem_read, mem_write, and reg_write cleared. Decoder legality rules\nand the is_illegal value of every valid instruction remain unchanged.\n\nCompute load-use comparisons directly from the unmasked fetched source\nfields. Qualify the hazard with imem_ready, the existing EX load control,\nand nonzero rd, preserving the old unavailable-fetch behavior. Do not\nqualify these comparisons with IF valid, flush_if, or redirect: IF valid\nincludes the late redirect and would recreate the path. A valid EX load\nand an EX branch/jump redirect are mutually exclusive under the existing\nvalidated decoder. Keep the current hazard priorities: dmem backpressure\nand \n…[12887 of 15959 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e0119f7e3c9569d9]…\nrototype results, not a completed orchestrator evaluation.\nPredict an integer 8 percent improvement with high confidence in\nthe measured timing/throughput effect. The final implementation must\nstill rerun the unchanged formal and evaluation gates and obtain\nfresh median vendor timing; another implementation's mapping may vary.\nAt unchanged cycles, median Fmax must exceed about 74.964 MHz and\nfitness must exceed 178.59404 iter/sec to clear the acceptance gate.\n\nValidate strict lint, exact real M-extension results, all existing\npipeline/decoder/register-file tests and unchanged formal/cosim gates.\nVerify the formatted bits use the correct youngest forwarded source,\nstay paired through dmem/divider holds and reset/flush correctly.\nRun canonical 2K CoreMark with both bus-stall flags, all required\nCRCs/UART validation, memory bounds and start/stop markers, then\nmeasure median Gowin Fmax times actual bracketed iterations/cycle.\nModify only allowed RTL/tests and preserve all hard invariants.\n\nImplementation notes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
