{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"agent_message","text":"Registering PC+4 improves one placement to 83.314 MHz, though it remains below acceptance. I’m extending that same optimization to register PC+immediate destinations for branches and JAL at ID/EX. This removes target addition from EX recovery feedback while keeping branch resolution and JALR in EX."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_93", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r7s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r7s0',\n 'title':'Prepare sequential and PC-relative destinations before execute feedback',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion reaches 194.25 iterations/second at 81.537 MHz with\n4197447 canonical stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. Its balanced branch\ncomparator removed the former deep comparison path, but EX recovery,\npredictor training and result forwarding still share full-width PC\narithmetic. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior micro_opt attempts addressed\narithmetic sharing, redirect masking and multiplier operand formatting;\nnone prepared the sequential and direct control-flow destinations at\nthe existing ID/EX boundary. The rejected registered-recovery and extra\nfetch/decode stages changed latency; this proposal keeps both unchanged.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Perform one local PC-arithmetic preparation optimization at the existing\nID/EX boundary. Add pc_plus4 and pc_target to id_ex_t. In ID's existing\nnormal capture arm, register pc_plus4 = in.pc + 32'd4 and pc_target =\nin.pc + imm, using the fetched instruction's full-width PC and decoded\nimmediate. These fields advance, reset, flush and hold together with\nthe current instruction, operands, controls and prediction metadata.\nCompute them unconditionally on the existing capture edge rather than\nadding branch-specific write enables or another pipeline stage.\n\nIn EX, use registered pc_plus4 for JAL/JALR link forwarding and EX/MEM\nwriteback, and for architectural sequential next-PC on ordinary,\nnot-taken and trapped instructions. Use registered pc_target as the\nconditional branch destination and direct JAL destination, including\nalignment checks, resolved target reporting, predictor training and\ntarget-mismatch comparison. Preserve JALR's existing finalized rs1 plus\nimmediate sum and bit-zero clearing. Resolve branch conditions in EX\nwith the accepted eight-four-bit balanced comparator. EX acceptance,\nrecovery timing, actual direction, misalignment trapping, stale-hit\nrecovery and once-only training retain their current definitions.\n\nThis moves independent PC additions ahead of an existing register\nboundary so they need not lie in EX's result/redirect/training feedback.\nIt preserves the five-stage organization, single-cycle ordinary and\nmultiply instructions, current divider, predictor policy and capacity,\nforwarding priority, load-use bubbles and every bus handshake. Keep\nAUIPC and all non-control-flow ALU/address arithmetic unchanged. Preserve\nfull 32-bit modulo arithmetic; do not truncate PCs to the benchmark's\nworking set, assume a fixed ROM or specialize to observed branches.\nThe RVFI next-PC and JAL/JALR result must still be exact for arbitrary\ninstruction streams, wraparound, illegal instructions and misalignment.\n\nAn isolated partial prototype registering only pc_plus4 measures\n83.314 MHz on Gowin placement option one, versus 81.537 MHz champion\nmedian, with 4553 logic cells and 1887 registers. This partial result is\nonly a 2.18 percent Fmax gain and does not clear acceptance. The proposed\ncandidate additionally prepares pc_target, removing another full-width\nadder from accepted direct control-flow feedback. Its complete median\nFmax and canonical cycle count must be measured before claiming a win.\nEstimate an eight percent fitness improvement with low confidence;\nextra target registers and the fetch/immediate-to-target capture path\nmay offset the gain. At unchanged cycles median Fmax must exceed about\n85.29 MHz to clear the champion by the required 4.6 percent.\n\nKeep all existing pipeline assertions, including full-zero ID/EX reset\nand flush checks and complete-bundle stability while held. Add checks\nthat prepared destinations stay paired with their instruction through\nload-use, imem/dmem backpressure, division, reset and recovery. Exercise\nall six branch conditions, forward/backward direct targets, taken and\nnot-taken misaligned branches, JAL/JALR links and changing JALR operands,\nwraparound and stale predictor hits. Require exact source/result/PC\nRVFI fields, monotonically consecutive order and once-only stores.\nRun unchanged formal/cosim gates and canonical stalled CoreMark with\nall CRCs, UART completion, bounds and start/stop markers, then score\nactual median Gowin Fmax times measured iterations/cycle. Preserve the\nnret=1 IO shape and every hard invariant and don't-touch file.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add full-width pc_plus4 and pc_target fields to id_ex_t only. Preserve all existing fields and the retirement-width contract.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Register in.pc+4 and in.pc+imm unconditionally in the existing normal\nID/EX capture arm. Preserve the current full-register reset/flush/invalid\nbubble behavior and hold every prepared field with the full bundle.\nDo not add stages, write-enable qualifiers or late operand refresh.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace EX's PC+4 uses with in.pc_plus4 and branch/direct-JAL PC+imm\nuses with in.pc_target. Use the prepared values consistently for links,\nnext-PC, alignment, predictor updates, target comparison and EX/MEM\nmetadata. Preserve JALR rs1+imm, AUIPC/ALU/address arithmetic, balanced\nbranch comparisons, trap controls, accepted redirects and all holds.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every architectural and existing reset/flush/held-bundle check.\nAdd directed prepared-PC pairing checks through backpressure, load-use,\ndivision, recovery and reset; cover signed direct offsets, all branch\npredicates and misalignment outcomes, links, indirect targets, stale\nhits and full-width wraparound. Keep exact RVFI, order and store checks.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=76))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Rewritten and validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
