he unsigned remainder.\n\nBuild each active subtractor from bit generate g=(~x)&y and propagate\np=~(x^y), with borrow-in zero. Combine (g,p) through a balanced prefix\ntree, preferably with four-bit local groups and a balanced group tree,\nto compute every bit's borrow and the final borrow without a serial\nfull-width carry chain. Difference bits are x^y^borrow_in. Both the\nquotient decision and the selected residual must use these lookahead\nresults; computing a separate ripple subtraction would retain the\nbottleneck. Constant step widths and divisor-overflow checks should\nkeep the network triangular rather than using 32 full-width rows.\n\nSelect quotient versus remainder before the final signed correction.\nNegate a signed quotient when operand signs \n…[27129 of 30201 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f1c1c033775d930d]…\nanced branch comparisons, direction/target recovery,\npredictor policy/training, illegal and misalignment traps, memory\nbackpressure and nret=1 IO/retirement. Keep all existing assertions and\nchecks, including zero bubbles and full-bundle stability under holds.\nVerify all fourteen groups, all M-extension variants, youngest-writer\nsources, x0, load dependencies and reset/recovery during stalled execution.\nRun real arithmetic vectors, strict real/ALTOPS lint, unchanged formal and\nretirement cosim, then canonical stalled CoreMark with exact CRC/UART,\nbounds and marker-bracketed cycles. Score actual median Gowin Fmax times\nmeasured iterations/cycle; modify only allowed RTL and cocotb tests.\n\nNOTES: \nhyp-20261005-002-r7s1 | structural | regression | fitness 196.38 | MHz 82.428 | cycles 4197447 | Bank the register file into shallow asynchronous distributed memories\nhyp-20261005-003-r7s2 | predictor | regression | fitness 199.92 | MHz 83.917 | cycles 4197447 | Register direct predictor verification targets before EX\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
