{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"Simpler branch-predicate selection is the first promising result: 83.438 MHz in one Gowin placement, about 2.3% above the champion. That is still below the acceptance threshold. I’m refining that single angle and checking equivalence before measuring all placement options.\n"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,shutil\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r8s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r8s0',\n 'title':'Factor branch predicate selection around the balanced comparator',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The successful four-bit balanced branch comparator removed a long comparison chain, but EX branch-resolution feedback still crosses predictor training, recovery and ID capture. Registered grouped ALU selection regressed to 73.948 MHz; recent register-file banking and target registration were below acceptance. Local probes reproduced the champion at 81.537 MHz and rejected explicit carry lookahead, ALU comparison/shifter rewrites, early general operand capture and instruction masking changes. The strongest remaining measured micro-optimization is simplifying selection among branch predicates without changing the comparator, pipeline or predictor policy.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace EX's six-arm branch predicate result mux with a factored function of the existing registered branch_op bits. Retain the exact eight-four-bit balanced lexicographic comparator and its unsigned less-than/equality roots. Preserve signed_lt = sign_difference ? rs1_sign : unsigned_lt. Compute base = branch_op[2] ? (branch_op[1] ? unsigned_lt : signed_lt) : equality, then branch_cond = base XOR branch_op[0]. Explicitly return zero for reserved branch_op values 010 and 011. Thus BEQ/BNE share equality, BLT/BGE share signed magnitude, and BLTU/BGEU share unsigned magnitude, with one common predicate inversion. Use the existing control flops, add no registers or pipeline stage, and keep branch_taken qualification unchanged.\n\nThis is one local branch-result selection optimization, not a predictor redesign. Keep current comparator leaves/tree, PC/target arithmetic, prediction verification, direction/target mismatch factoring, alignment faults and trapping PC behavior, immediate accepted-EX recovery and once-only training. Preserve all ALU operations, native multiplier operand preparation, restoring divider and sticky completion, finalized source forwarding, every stall/flush rule, exact RV32IM and ALTOPS semantics, nret=1/top-level IO, consecutive retirement, bounded memory and all unchanged correctness contracts. Modify only the listed allowed RTL and cocotb tests.\n\nAn isolated implementation of this exact factored topology measures 83.438 MHz on Gowin placement option one, versus a freshly reproduced 81.537 MHz champion on that same option. Resources are 4715 logic cells, 1857 registers, 32 LUT-RAM units, five BSRAMs and two DSPs. The gain is 2.33 percent in this single placement; it is not a scored median or an accepted champion replacement. Predict an integer two percent fitness gain with medium confidence pending full validation. At unchanged cycles median Fmax must exceed approximately 85.29 MHz and fitness must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec to clear the required 4.6 percent gate. Smaller gains must not be accepted.\n\nProve unsigned/signed/equality predicate selection equivalent for all operands and all eight branch_op encodings. Retain existing directed and randomized branch cases and every pipeline assertion, especially full-bundle clearing on flush, stable held operands, truthful trap/training metadata, changing JALR targets, stale hits, wrong-path stores and retirement order. Run strict real/ALTOPS lint, the unchanged nret=1 formal gate and full retirement cosim, then canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/bracketing validation and every vendor placement option. Score only median Gowin Fmax times actual marker-bracketed iterations/cycle; another ALU or routing path may cap the gain.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':2,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace only the branch_op case mux with the precise factored predicate and reserved-encoding zero guard described above. Reuse the existing compare_lt/compare_eq roots and signed_lt. Keep all arithmetic, targets, traps, producer enables, predictor metadata, acceptance, immediate recovery and pipeline registers unchanged.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain every existing assertion and all branch boundary/random, stall, trap, predictor, forwarding and retirement cases. Add directed predicate-pair checks for BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU with equal/different signs and decisive high/low groups, exercising both bus stalls. Require equivalent exact RVFI next PCs and once-only side effects. Preserve the unmodified formal, cosim, canonical CoreMark and vendor fitness gates.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated schema-valid hypothesis:',p)\nprobe=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/3690d99c/r8s0_probe')\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/test',probe/'branch_factor/test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\n(probe/'branch_factor'/'predicate_miter.sv').write_text('''module predicate_miter(input [31:0] a,b,input [2:0] op,output bad);\nwire [15:1] lt,eq;\nfor(genvar g=0;g<8;g=g+1) begin\n assign lt[8+g]=a[4*g +: 4]<b[4*g +: 4];\n assign eq[8+g]=a[4*g +: 4]==b[4*g +: 4];\nend\nfor(genvar g=1;g<8;g=g+1) begin\n assign lt[g]=lt[2*g+1] | (eq[2*g+1]&lt[2*g]);\n assign eq[g]=eq[2*g+1]&eq[2*g];\nend\nwire slt=(a[31]\"'^b[31])?a[31]:lt[1];\nwire factored=(!op[2]&&op[1])?1'\"'b0:((op[2]?(op[1]?lt[1]:slt):eq[1])\"'^op[0]);\nreg reference;\nalways @* case(op)\n0:reference=(a==b); 1:reference=(a!=b);\n4:reference=($signed(a)<$signed(b)); 5:reference=($signed(a)>=$signed(b));\n6:reference=(a<b); 7:reference=(a>=b); default:reference=0;\nendcase\nassign bad=factored!=reference;\nendmodule\n'\"''')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
