{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport json\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/1602ad9d')\ndef run(width):\n p=root/f'carry{width}_proto'\n r=build(Path.cwd(),p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',1,p/'timing_p1')\n (p/'timing.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\n print('WIDTH',width,json.dumps(r),flush=True)\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2) as pool:\n list(pool.map(run,(4,8)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r9s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Balanced block carry lookahead for ALU ADD and SUB'\nh['motivation']='''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 canonical stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. Recent timing paths alternate between IF/RF/ID operand capture and EX arithmetic feeding ID forwarding. The current ALU uses native full-width ADD and SUB followed by result selection; long carry dependencies can consume timing budget in the closed EX-result-to-ID-capture path. LESSONS.md is absent. Relevant micro_opt attempts show grouped ALU result selection regressed and branch predicate factoring gained only 2.33 percent. A local arithmetic topology change can shorten a real hardware path while preserving every instruction latency.'''\nh['hypothesis']='''Replace only the base ALU ADD and SUB arithmetic with explicit balanced block carry-lookahead networks. Divide operands into eight four-bit groups. Independently compute each group's WIDTH+1-bit carry-zero local sum, group generate from its carry-out and group propagate from the AND of bitwise operand XORs. Form all group carry inputs with a three-level constant-index parallel prefix over (generate,propagate), using G_combined=G_high|(P_high&G_low) and P_combined=P_high&P_low. Correct each low four-bit local sum with its one-bit group carry-in. ADD uses a,b and initial carry zero; SUB uses a,~b and initial carry one. Use separate combinational instances so ALU opcode decoding is absent from operand inversion and initial carry. The result remains full-width arithmetic modulo 2\"'^32 for every operand pair.\n\nKeep the existing ALU operation case/output selection, operand routing, producer forwarding, finalized source flops, branch comparator and target calculation, native multiplier, divider/ALTOPS formulas, decoder legality/traps, interlocks and all pipeline registers unchanged. Helpers may live inside alu.sv to avoid source-list changes. There is no extra stage, request, clock enable, arithmetic latency or false dependency; this is solely a local base-adder implementation change. Do not apply the rewrite to the divider recurrence, predictor target adder, PC increment or RVFI-only arithmetic. Preserve nret=1/top-level IO, exact bus/stall acceptance, complete cleared bubbles, held operands, retirement order/progress, memory bounds, CoreMark CRCs/completion and marker timing.\n\nEstimate a six percent gain with low confidence before measurement. Native FPGA carry chains may outperform the prefix network or RF/control paths may dominate. At unchanged canonical cycles median Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 85.29 MHz and fitness must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec to clear the 4.6 percent acceptance gate. Prove the adder/subtractor equivalent for unrestricted operands, retain all existing arithmetic/pipeline assertions and unchanged formal/cosim gates, and obtain fresh median vendor timing with actual canonical stalled bracket cycles.'\"'''\nh['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Implement separate explicit four-bit-block ADD and SUB helpers with balanced group carry prefix and local carry correction; replace only ALU_ADD/ALU_SUB result expressions. Preserve every other operation, multiplier ports, divider handshake, real/ALTOPS behavior, operation default and module interface.'},{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain every existing arithmetic assertion. Add carry/borrow propagation across each group boundary, all-zero/all-one and signed extremes, modular overflow, alternating patterns and deterministic random ADD/SUB references. Prove unrestricted combinational equivalence and run unchanged pipeline/formal/cosim plus canonical stalled CoreMark validation before vendor median fitness scoring.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis saved and schema validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
