{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/1602ad9d/branch_trap_factoring')\nshutil.copytree('/srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/1602ad9d/ex_producer/rtl',p/'rtl',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/test',p/'test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nf=p/'rtl/core.sv';s=f.read_text().replace('.update_legal(predictor_update_legal)', '.update_legal(\"'!id_ex_w.ctrl.is_illegal)'\"')\ns=s.replace('  logic predictor_update_legal, predictor_update_taken;','  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\\\\n  logic predictor_update_legal;\\\\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\\\\n  logic predictor_update_taken;');f.write_text(s)\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r9s0',\n 'title':'Remove redundant branch-trap qualification from EX feedback enables',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz with 4197447 canonical stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. Its EX feedback and ID operand capture paths are close to the timing limit. Taken-branch misalignment currently feeds ctrl_with_trap, which feeds both EX producer validity and predictor allocation legality. Those consumers already have independent conditions that make this branch-trap term redundant: validated conditional branches never write an rd, and predictor allocation already requires the resolved target to be aligned. Removing the two redundant outcome-dependent qualifications together can reduce the branch comparison's control fanout while preserving identical architectural behavior and predictor policy. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior micro_opt ALU predecode and several operand-selection/arithmetic prototypes regressed; branch predicate factoring gained only 2.33 percent. Isolated removal of either qualification measured 80.951 MHz and 79.915 MHz on placement option one, respectively, below the champion. The proposed joint factoring has not yet established a scored win; it targets the common branch-trap cone left live by either isolated edit.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Perform one Boolean dependency optimization of the EX feedback enables: remove taken-branch-misalignment qualification where other existing guards already imply it. Keep the complete architectural ctrl_with_trap calculation and every retiring trap/control bit unchanged.\n\nFor EX producer_w_en, use in.valid && in.ctrl.reg_write && \"'!in.ctrl.is_illegal && !misalign_jump && (in.rd!=0) && !in.ctrl.mem_read && (!is_div || div_done). This equals the existing predicate for every decoder-generated control bundle because a conditional branch has reg_write=0, and the only EX alignment fault of a register-writing instruction is a misaligned JAL/JALR. Keep the JAL/JALR guard intact. Do not remove effective MEM load-misalignment qualification or permit unfinished division forwarding. Producer data and EX > MEM > RF forwarding remain unchanged.\n\nFor the branch_predictor instance'\"'s update_legal input, connect the original registered decoder legality, \"'!id_ex_w.ctrl.is_illegal, instead of EX'\"'s outcome-dependent effective trap legality. Retain the predictor's existing full-width update target range/alignment checks without weakening them. Allocation requires update_legal && (update_branch || update_jump) && target_in_range, where target_in_range already requires update_target[1:0]==0. That target is exactly the EX branch or jump target tested by misalign_fault. Consequently, whenever allocation is possible, no branch/jump misalignment fault exists and decoded legality equals effective legality. Misaligned targets still follow exactly the original matching-only invalidation path for both taken and not-taken branches. Ordinary/illegal instructions still invalidate only their own matching row. Counter transitions, target/tag writes, jump metadata, allocation, invalidation, reset and lookup/update visibility must remain identical for all inputs reachable from validated decode.\n\nPreserve the existing EX predictor_update_legal signal as a truthful effective-legality monitor for tests, even though the predictor now receives the equivalent allocation qualifier. Mark only that unused internal monitor appropriately for strict synthesis lint; do not change any trap assertion or monitor expectation. Architectural misalign_branch/misalign_jump, ctrl_with_trap, PC-next behavior, reg_write suppression on jump traps and original RVFI traps remain unchanged. The optimization must not alter taken outcomes, prediction policy or training acceptance/cycles, target arithmetic, storage, capacity, table indexing or recovery. No new stage, delay, speculative acceptance, prevalidated target register or altered bubble representation is part of this proposal.\n\nKeep all current ID/EX and EX/MEM reset/flush/hold behavior, complete zero bubbles, finalized operands, true RV32IM and ALTOPS arithmetic, multiplier/divider ports and completion protocols, validated decoder defaults, memory handshake acceptance, nret=1/top-level IO, retirement order/progress, bounds, canonical CRCs, completion text and MMIO brackets. Modify only allowed RTL and cocotb tests.\n\nEstimate a six percent fitness gain with low confidence pending fresh median timing. The joint change may let synthesis remove the common branch-trap dependence from both high-fanout feedback consumers, while single edits leave it live through the other consumer. Another ALU or RF path may dominate and the combined implementation may regress; do not claim measured acceptance without a completed median vendor run. Expect identical canonical CoreMark cycles, but score actual bracketed iterations/cycle and median Gowin Fmax. The gate requires fitness above 203.1855 iter/sec, approximately 85.29 MHz at 4197447 cycles. Prove both predicate equivalences under the unchanged decoder's reachable controls, run all existing unit/formal/cosim gates, then validate canonical stalled CoreMark and vendor fitness.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Factor EX producer enable using original decode legality/reg_write and jump-misalignment suppression instead of ctrl_with_trap branch outcome. Preserve effective ctrl_with_trap and predictor_update_legal monitor, all actual traps, producer data, divider availability, EX acceptance and architectural outputs.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Feed only the predictor allocation-legal input from the registered original decode legality. Keep the effective EX legality signal available unchanged for existing monitor assertions, adding a narrow unused-signal annotation if strict lint requires it. Preserve every predictor target guard, control/target wire, top-level port, hazard and retirement path.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain every existing assertion, especially truthful effective predictor legality and misalignment traps. Add comparisons of old/new EX write eligibility on all decoder-generated instruction kinds and old/new predictor allocation transactions, taken/not-taken misaligned branch targets, aligned and misaligned JAL/JALR, stale tag matches/misses, ordinary/illegal instructions and reset/holds. Require identical target/direction predictions, updates, recoveries, architectural sources/results, order, stores and cycle behavior. Run strict real/ALTOPS lint, existing arithmetic/decoder/predictor/pipeline tests, unchanged formal and eight retirement cosims, canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/brackets and fresh median vendor fitness.'}\n ]}\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r9s0.yaml');f.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False));jsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print('Final joint branch-trap factoring hypothesis saved and schema validated')\nPY\npython3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all,summarize\nimport json\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/1602ad9d/branch_trap_factoring')\nr=build_all(Path.cwd(),p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',p/'timing')\n(p/'timing.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(summarize(r)),flush=True)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
