{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r10s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Pipeline DSP partial products with dependency-only bubbles'\nh['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':1,'confidence':'medium'}\nh['hypothesis']='''Change multiplication to a fully pipelined, in-order MEM-available producer.\nLaunch four DSP-sized partial products directly from the existing finalized\nID/EX operands and registered sign-extension bits. Capture all partials at\nthe EX/MEM boundary; recombine and select the architectural result only\nin MEM. Exclude multiplication from current-EX forwarding and use one\nload-style dependency bubble only when the next encoded source matches\nits nonzero destination. Independent instructions and independent multiplies\ncontinue issuing every cycle. This is one change to multiplication execution\nstructure and its necessary dependency interlock.\n\nDecompose each prepared signed 33-bit operand into unsigned low 16 bits\nand signed high 17 bits: A=a_lo+(a_hi<<16), B=b_lo+(b_hi<<16).\nCompute p00=a_lo*b_lo as unsigned 32 bits; p01=a_lo*b_hi and\np10=a_hi*b_lo as signed 34 bits, explicitly zero-extending each unsigned\nlow operand to signed 17 bits; p11=a_hi*b_hi is signed 34 bits.\nThe existing sign flops make MULH signed/signed, MULHSU signed/unsigned,\nand MULHU unsigned/unsigned. MUL uses the same decomposition's low half.\nThere is no full-width native multiplier, unsigned-product sign correction,\nmultiplier request FSM, preliminary capture stage or global multiply wait.\n\nRegister these four raw partials in their own unreset EX/MEM payload flops.\nUpdate them on every \"'!stall edge, including harmless invalid EX bubbles;\nretain them on genuine older dmem backpressure. Keep reset, division-wait\nand bubble clearing on the original instruction metadata and validity.\nPayload bits on an invalid transaction are unobservable: producer enables,\nretirement and memory effects still require valid controls. A valid held\ntransaction retains its paired product and finalized architectural operands.\nDo not reset or clear DSP payloads through the branch/divider acceptance\ncone. All valid operations capture metadata and products on the same edge.\n\nReconstruct the low 64 product bits modulo 2''^64 after this register.\nUse four 64-bit terms: zero_extend(p00), sign_extend(p01)<<16,\nsign_extend(p10)<<16, and {p11[31:0],32'\"'b0}. Compress the first three\nterms with one carry-save XOR/majority layer, compress its sum/carry with\nthe fourth term using a second layer, then add the final 64-bit sum and\ncarry once. Each majority carry is shifted left one bit within 64 bits.\nThe selected implementation uses this complete carry-save reconstruction;\ndo not replace it with the slower tested narrow split or separately\nassembled low-result network. Select [31:0] for MUL and [63:32] for the\nthree high variants. Use the selected result for MEM-to-ID forwarding\nand capture it in MEM/WB.alu_result. WB and retirement stay in place.\nOrdinary ALU/address/link results continue using EX/MEM.alu_result.\n\nExpose raw partial products separately from alu.out and remove all real\nmultiplication from the ordinary EX ALU result/bypass cone. EX producer_w_en\nexcludes every multiply, so an unfinished multiply never forwards an older\nsame-rd value as its own result. Generalize the existing load-use interlock\nto a valid legal multiply in ID/EX. Preserve conservative encoded-source\nmatching and x0 exclusion. On a match, hold fetch, bubble ID/EX, and let\nthe multiply advance to EX/MEM; next cycle MEM supplies the product.\nWithout a match, issue normally. Preserve youngest EX > MEM > RF priority,\nWB write-first reads, exact raw RVFI operands and their stability on holds.\n\nGenuine dmem stalls take precedence over a dependency bubble and hold both\nEX/MEM metadata/products and ID/EX. Re-evaluate dependencies on acceptance.\nOlder MEM/WB drains once. Keep the iterative divider and its sticky completion,\nindependent progress and once-only consume protocol unchanged. Keep immediate\naccepted-EX recovery and predictor training, including stale predictions on\nordinary multiply instructions. Recovery overrides younger source-bit holds;\nwrong-path multiplies never retire or create architectural effects. Preserve\nthe predictor, balanced branch comparator, ordinary instruction latency,\nload-use behavior and both memory handshake contracts.\n\nPreserve every exact multiplication RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formula F using\nthe ordinary finalized architectural operands: p00=F, p01=p10=0,\np11={2'b0,F}. The same registered reconstruction then produces {F,F},\nso low/high selection returns F with the real hardware's dependency timing.\nChange no ALTOPS formula, formal wrapper, property, depth or configuration.\nReal builds always use the four native partial products. Adapt internal ALU\ntests to reconstruct the exported partial result while retaining all existing\nexact reference assertions, formatted-operand isolation and random/boundary\ncoverage. Preserve nret=1, all top-level IO, legality/traps, consecutive RVFI\norder, forward progress, memory bounds, CRCs, completion text and markers.\n\nAn isolated prototype of exactly this topology measures Gowin placements\n0/1/2 at 74.907, 82.643 and 82.643 MHz: median 82.643 MHz. Placement-0\nresources are 4762 logic cells, 1864 registers, 32 LUT-RAM units, five\nBSRAMs and two DSPs. The unchanged stalled CoreMark harness validates every\ncanonical CRC and completion text, reaches EBREAK in bounds with both\nmarkers, and measures 4232929 bracket cycles. This is 35482 extra cycles,\n0.8453 percent above 4197447, rather than the earlier every-multiply hold.\nMeasured fitness is 195.2383 iter/sec, 0.5088 percent above 194.25.\n\nStrict lint passes in real and ALTOPS builds. All eight unchanged retirement\ncosims pass: selftest and random1/2/3, each zero-wait and with both stalls.\nAdapted exact arithmetic tests, the dedicated ALTOPS test and all 34 pipeline\ntests pass; only internal result observation and explicit multiply-dependency\nlatency expectations change, with all architectural assertions retained.\nAll 53 unchanged nret=1 formal checks pass in an isolated copy of the original\nframework; the shared upstream framework and contract files are untouched.\nFull real-arithmetic formal-deep was not run. Final implementation must repeat\nthese gates and add the directed pipeline cases listed below.\n\nExpected integer gain is one percent with medium confidence. This measured\nprototype DOES NOT clear the required 4.6 percent acceptance margin; do not\npresent it as a demonstrated champion replacement. At its measured cycles,\nmedian Fmax must exceed approximately 86.007 MHz and fitness must exceed\n203.1855 iter/sec to be accepted. Remaining ordinary ALU, register access and\nbranch/predictor feedback still constrain timing. A resettable full-product\npipeline, forced register preservation, narrow recombination and duplicated\ncombinational low-MUL bypass timed worse and are excluded. Score fresh median\nGowin timing times actual canonical stalled bracket throughput; neither a\nsmall placement change nor timing alone establishes a win. Change only\nallowed RTL and cocotb tests, and no evaluation-contract file.\n'''\ndesc={\n'rtl/core_pkg.sv':'''Add unsigned 32-bit mul_p00 and signed 34-bit mul_p01/mul_p10/mul_p11\nfields to ex_mem_t. Retain all architectural metadata, ctrl_t and the\nexisting MEM/WB result contract. No new instruction stage or retirement\nchannel is required.''',\n'rtl/alu.sv':'''Replace the full signed native multiplier with the four DSP-sized\npartial products described above, exported separately from ordinary out.\nKeep prepared mul_a/mul_b launch inputs; remove multiplication from out.\nPreserve base arithmetic and divider unchanged. ALTOPS exports p00=F,\np01=p10=0 and p11={2'b0,F} for each exact original multiplication formula.''',\n'rtl/ex_stage.sv':'''Capture four unreset raw partials on \"'!stall in a separate payload\nregister bank and override the corresponding output-bundle fields with\nthat bank. Reset/bubbles clear original metadata/validity; dmem holds\nretain both. Exclude all multiply variants from current-EX forwarding.\nPreserve ordinary/link/address results, division waits, accepted immediate\nrecovery/training, finalized RVFI operands and all metadata pairing.\nIntroduce no multiplier FSM, global multiply wait or extra instruction stage.'\"''',\n'rtl/mem_stage.sv':'''Reconstruct the registered product modulo 2\"'^64 using two XOR/majority\ncarry-save layers and one final 64-bit addition. Select low/high half\nby the saved validated multiplication operation. Use the result for\nMEM forwarding and MEM/WB.alu_result, retaining all load extraction,\nbyte lanes, memory gating, traps, RVFI and once-only retirement behavior.'\"''',\n'rtl/hazard_unit.sv':'''Generalize the one-cycle unavailable-producer source dependency to\nloads and valid legal multiplies in EX. A match holds fetch, bubbles\nID/EX and lets EX/MEM advance; no match allows normal issue. Keep\nconservative encoded-source comparisons, x0 exclusion, genuine dmem\nhold priority, immediate recovery priority and the divider protocol.''',\n'rtl/core.sv':'''Wire the qualified current-EX multiply producer-latency flag to the\ndependency interlock. Preserve the existing forwarding topology,\nall top-level ports, nret=1, RVFI and retirement ordering.''',\n 'test/test_alu.py':'''Adapt internal result observation to the exported signed partial\nproducts while retaining every existing exact RV32M reference assertion,\nboundary/random vector, formatted-operand isolation and ALTOPS test.\nCheck full prepared 33-bit inputs, low overflow and all high signedness\nvariants. Retain all ordinary and divider tests without weakened checks.''',\n 'test/test_pipeline.py':'''Update only explicit latency expectations affected by immediate\nmultiply dependencies; retain every architectural assertion. Add\nindependent back-to-back multiplies proving one-per-cycle issue,\nimmediate/spaced consumers of every variant, dependent multiply chains,\nsimultaneous EX/MEM/WB writes to the same rd and x0. Cover consumers in\nALU, branch, JALR, load/store address, store data and division; require\none bubble for direct dependencies and none for independent consumers.\nExercise dmem holds at partial capture and MEM forwarding, imem stalls,\nreset, stale predictions and wrong-path products. Verify exact RVFI\nsources/results/PC/traps/order, stable requests, once-only stores and\nbounded progress. Run unchanged lint, unit, nret=1 formal and retirement\ncosim gates, then canonical CRC/completion/bounds/marker validation and\nfresh median vendor timing. Acceptance still requires more than 4.6\npercent fitness improvement.'''}\nfor c in h['changes']:c['description']=desc[c['file']]+'\\\\n'\nclass LiteralDumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef rep(d,s):return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nLiteralDumper.add_representer(str,rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=LiteralDumper,sort_keys=False,width=95))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis is schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
