heir existing single-cycle paths. Each ordinary division performs 32 bounded recurrence cycles, with separate bounded operand normalization and result sign-correction states if needed. Each recurrence uses one 33-bit trial subtraction and a borrow-controlled selection, rather than a chain of 32 division stages. No synthesizable / or % operation may remain in the normal hardware ALU or divider.  Accept a request exactly once for a valid division instruction when its forwarded operands are available and older data-memory backpressure permits launch. Snapshot both forwarded source values and the operation; preserve those same values for RVFI even after the older forwarding producers drain. Hold fetch and ID/EX while di\n…[26384 of 29456 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:29771fe0cb5e261b]…\noduct payload and EX/MEM transaction metadata. Existing reset/flush/divider-wait behavior still clears validity and side-effect controls. Invalid payload bits are unobservable; each valid multiplication's product and original metadata must refer to the same acceptance edge. Keep the normal EX/MEM register protocol unchanged.  Remove multiplication from current-EX architectural forwarding and from the ordinary combinational ALU output. In MEM, select product[31:0] for MUL or product[63:32] for MULH/MULHSU/MULHU using the saved validated op. Use that result for MEM-to-ID forwarding and MEM/WB.alu_result. There is only a low/h\nhyp-20261005-003-r11s2 predictor BTB-free direct prediction with bounded target arithmetic\n  outcome= regression fitness= 174.22 fmax= 73.211 cycles= 4202272 path= {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.is_auipc_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_product_65_s1', 'slack_ns': -7.858, 'arrival_ns': 17.932, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
