o not qualify address capture with io_dmemReady\nbeyond the existing EX/MEM stall. Non-memory idle bus addresses are\nirrelevant to memory acceptance and must not create read/write enables.\n\nIn MEM use effective_addr consistently for dmem_addr, alignment-fault\ndetection, byte-lane masks, load extraction and aligned RVFI mem_addr.\nPreserve replicated store data, read/write suppression on misalignment,\nload sign extension, trap/writeback suppression and held MEM/WB\nforwarding fields. Preserve full-width architectural addresses; no\nbenchm\n…[14086 of 17158 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5b055f050da2ba60]…\nuation-contract change. The optimization is physically separating multiplier launch storage from general operand storage at an existing boundary.\n\nPredict six percent fitness improvement with low confidence pending the final isolated prototype measurements. Extra storage and decoded multiply-enable fanout may offset improved routing, and residual EX/predictor/ID paths may remain limiting. Do not claim a demonstrated win from this estimate. Expect identical canonical CoreMark cycle count, but score actual bracketed cycles and all three fresh Gowin placement options. Acceptance requires fitness above 203.1855 iter/sec, roughly 85.286 MHz at 4197447 cycles. Run unchanged correctness gates; all hardware multiply variants must remain exact, including dependent multiply chains and signed high halves.\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_4_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_product_65_s1', 'slack_ns': -8.042, 'arrival_ns': 18.116, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_predictor', 'cpu/u_id']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
