{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nroot=Path.cwd();base=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/e3e10f46/r14q4plain')\nf=base/'formal';f.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nfor name in ['run_all.sh','wrapper_si.sv','checks_si.cfg']:shutil.copy2(root/'formal'/name,f/name)\nfor name in ['checks','insns']:shutil.copytree(root/'formal/riscv-formal'/name,f/'riscv-formal'/name,dirs_exist_ok=True)\nPY\nRTL_DIR=rtl CORE_NAME=bench WRAPPER=/srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/e3e10f46/r14q4plain/formal/wrapper_si.sv JOBS=8 bash /srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/e3e10f46/r14q4plain/formal/run_all.sh /srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/e3e10f46/r14q4plain/formal/checks_si.cfg > /srv/hwebench/tmp/3d673a88/e3e10f46/r14q4plain/formal.out 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_65", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r14s1.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-002-r14s1',\n'title':'Decouple fetch with a compact registered four-entry instruction queue',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz with 4,197,447\nmarker-bracketed cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Structural r13s1's two-entry\nfall-through queue reduced cycles to 3,978,917 but lost timing through\noccupancy, fetch selection and the RF/ID read path, scoring 189.69.\nStructural r6s1's single registered decoded slot barely overlapped stalls.\nUse a deeper, compact registered raw-instruction FIFO to retain bus-stall\noverlap while removing fall-through selection from operand collection.\nPrior multiplier pipelines, delayed recovery and RF/bypass restructures\nhave not cleared the current acceptance margin.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the combinational IF/ID connection with exactly four elastic\nraw-instruction slots, with a permanently registered physical head and\nan independent fetch PC. This is one structural change to the fetch-to-\noperand boundary. Keep single issue, the current decoded-control and\nfinalized-operand ID/EX register, all execute units and retirement stages.\nThere is no empty fall-through, pointer-selected head or buffered operand.\n\nImplement a shift FIFO with explicit constant slot registers. Each payload\ncontains only the full PC, original instruction, predicted direction and\npredicted next address. Occupancy owns validity; the head payload drives ID\nwithout an empty/unready instruction-mask mux. Decode, immediate generation,\nRF reads and EX > MEM > WB/RF forwarding operate on this registered head.\nCapture finalized architectural operands only on actual ID/EX acceptance;\nencoded unused source fields retain their existing RVFI behavior.\n\nFetch accepts a ready response whenever space exists, including during\nload-use, division and genuine data-memory holds. Allow simultaneous head\nconsumption and refill even at full occupancy. Advance the fetch PC exactly\nonce per accepted response using that response's prediction. An unready bus\ncannot enqueue or advance PC, and a full unconsumed FIFO holds fetch.\nA valid buffered head can issue while imemReady is low. Compute load-use\nfrom that head's encoded source tags and preserve the existing conservative\nmatching, one bubble, x0 exclusion and youngest effective producer priority.\nDo not consume on a load-use bubble, held EX, reset or recovery.\n\nPartition speculative FIFO payload movement from committed queue state.\nCompute candidate head consumption from valid head and absence of ID hold,\nand candidate enqueue from imemReady and capacity after that consumption.\nThese payload shift/fill enables must not depend on late redirect/flush.\nIt is safe to move discarded payload on a redirect edge. Separately give\nreset and accepted EX recovery priority over occupancy and fetch-PC updates:\nreset clears occupancy and defines all payload words; recovery empties the\nqueue and sets the full architectural fetch destination. Candidate movements\non recovery never create a valid entry; subsequent target enqueue overwrites\nhead before it can issue. Normal cycles commit candidate transfers exactly\nonce. Retain the original priority flush at ID/EX so no wrong-path instruction\ncan execute, train the predictor, launch division, access memory or retire.\n\nPreserve immediate accepted-EX recovery, the exact 64-row predictor, full\nrange/alignment guards, old-row lookup/update behavior and once-only training.\nLookup stays at independent io_imemAddr. Save exactly the prediction used\nwhen each response was accepted and retain it through queue holds and later\ntraining. Recovery discards every younger queued entry and concurrent fetch,\neven during instruction backpressure. The target must enter through the new\nhead register on a later ready edge: one additional recovery cycle is the\nexplicit latency cost. Preserve stale ordinary and misaligned-trap recovery.\n\nGenuine dmem backpressure still holds the outstanding EX/MEM request and\nfinalized ID/EX operands; older WB drains once. Divider launch, independent\niteration, sticky completion and once-only consume remain unchanged. Keep\noriginal instruction decode and operand launch boundaries, RF storage/read\ncontract, multiplier sign preparation, branch comparison, arithmetic and\nall exact ALTOPS formulas. No extra ALU stage, delayed predictor maintenance,\nsource-mask bank or register-file rewrite is part of this proposal.\n\nAn isolated initial four-slot source-mask prototype was slower. The selected\ncompact topology removes those masks and all late recovery qualification from\nFIFO payload enables; use explicit slot registers instead of struct-array\nwrites for portable Yosys elaboration. Its placement-option-1 vendor timing\nis 80.084 MHz, with 4795 logic cells, 2246 registers, 32 LUT-RAM units,\nfive BSRAMs and two DSPs. This is a single placement, not a scored median.\nEight unchanged full-retirement cosims pass for selftest and random1/2/3,\nwith and without both stalls. Canonical stalled CoreMark validation passes.\nFinal median timing and full formal status must be checked before claiming\na win; no demonstrated champion replacement is claimed.\n\nPredict two percent fitness improvement with low confidence. Stall overlap\ncan offset the modest timing cost, but the acceptance threshold is stricter:\nactual iterations/cycle times median Gowin Fmax must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec.\nAt 4,032,021 timed cycles, median Fmax must exceed 81.92482 MHz. This is a\nmeasurement-guided structural candidate, and a subthreshold result is not an\naccepted improvement. Score fresh median vendor timing and actual canonical\nstalled CoreMark bracket cycles, never timing or placement noise alone.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and exact top-level memory/channel-0 RVFI ports, default-\nillegal decode, legality/misalignment traps, real RV32IM arithmetic, strict\nconsecutive retirement order, progress, memory bounds, canonical CRCs,\ncompletion text and timing markers. Run unchanged lint, unit architectural\nassertions, single-channel formal and full retirement cosim, then vendor\nfitness. Modify only allowed RTL/tests; preserve wrappers, formal settings,\nbenchmark sources, evaluator, core.yaml and every other contract file.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':2,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Add an independent fetch PC and four explicit compact shift-FIFO payload\nregisters. Present only registered head data, with occupancy-based validity.\nAccept ready responses during backend holds and permit full consume/refill.\nSeparate speculative payload enables from priority reset/recovery updates\nto committed occupancy and PC; keep discarded payload architecturally inert.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Connect true imem readiness and candidate head consumption to fetch.\nDrive decode, RF addressing, forwarding and load-use from the registered\nhead; keep predictor lookup at io_imemAddr and preserve all backend/RVFI\nwiring and top-level ports. Head validity replaces live imem readiness\nas the decode-availability condition.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'''Separate buffered-head availability and ID acceptance from independent\nfetch capacity. Preserve load-use bubbles, dmem/divider holds, WB drain\nand recovery priority. Derive speculative payload consumption from ID\nhold conditions without routing late flush into FIFO payload enables.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain architectural assertions and add registered queue lifecycle cases:\nempty fill, no live fall-through, full hold, simultaneous consume/refill,\niStall head drain, load/division/dmem overlap, poisoned unavailable data,\nprediction pairing, reset and redirects at every occupancy. Check exact\nRVFI sources/results/PC/order, once-only memory effects and progress.\nUpdate only explicit front-end latency expectations for registered head\nrecovery; preserve arithmetic, legality and side-effect checks.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated compact registered-queue YAML; schema validation passed.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
