sue EX stage around its\nrequest/response handshake. Keep RV32I arithmetic and all multiplication\noperations on their existing single-cycle paths. Each ordinary division\nperforms 32 bounded recurrence cycles, with separate bounded operand\nnormalization and result sign-correction states if needed. Each recurrence\nuses one 33-bit trial subtraction and a borrow-controlled selection, rather\nthan a chain of 32 division stages. No synthesizable / or % operation may\nremain in the normal hardware ALU or divider.\n\nAccept a request exactly once for a valid division instruction when its\nforwarded operands are available and older data-memory backpressure permits\nlaunch. Snapshot both forwarded source values and the operation; preserve\n…[5829 of 8901 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c99c8a7b351263e4]…\nke semantics and nret=1 remain\nintact. Taken branches and jumps gain one recovery bubble; that is the\nexplicit performance cost. Estimate a 20 percent fitness improvement if\nsplitting the measured control path raises Fmax enough to cover this cost.\nThis is a prediction, not a measured result. Compare marker-bracketed\nstalled CoreMark cycles and median Gowin Fmax against 104.12, requiring\nfitness above 108.91, rather than accepting Fmax improvement alone. Run\nexisting legality, arithmetic, pipeline, formal and retirement-cosim gates\nwithout modifying any wrapper, harness, benchmark or evaluation setting.\n\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-003-r2s2\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"title\": \"Small tagged target predictor with a short recovery path\", \"fitness\": 117.38, \"cycles\": 4197447, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.269, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.366, \"arrival_ns\": 26.661, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
