{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|Register branch recovery|registered partial-product|hyp-20261005-001-r3s0|hyp-20261005-003-r2s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Isolate division in a bounded multi-cycle execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline's median Fmax is only 5.442 MHz, with a reported 199.837 ns,\\n156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU. alu.sv implements signed\\nand unsigned division and remainder with combinational / and % operators.\\nThese unrolled arithmetic networks can constrain every instruction's\\nclock period, even when division is rare. The experiment history contains\\nonly the baseline retest and there is no LESSONS.md or prior structural\\nattempt. Removing the full-width combinational divider is the strongest\\nstructural opportunity suggested by this timing evidence.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline's median Fmax is only 5.442 MHz, with a reported 199.837 ns,\\n156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU. alu.sv implements signed\\nand unsigned division and remainder with combinational / and % operators.\\nThese unrolled arithmetic networks can constrain every instruction's\\nclock period, even when division is rare. The experiment history contains\\nonly the baseline retest and there is no LESSONS.md or prior structural\\nattempt. Removing the full-width combinational divider is the strongest\\nstructural opportunity suggested by this timing evidence.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one shared, registered radix-2\\nrestoring divider, and interlock the single-issue EX stage around its\\nrequest/response handshake. Keep RV32I arithmetic and all multiplication\\noperations on their existing single-cycle paths. Each ordinary division\\nperforms 32 bounded recurrence cycles, with separate bounded operand\\nnormalization and result sign-correction states if needed. Each recurrence\\nuses one 33-bit trial subtraction and a borrow-controlled selection, rather\\nthan a chain of 32 division stages. No synthesizable / or % operation may\\nremain in the normal hardware ALU or divider.\\n\\nAccept a request exactly once for a valid division instruction whe\n…[60185 of 63257 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:10bf71e9f3fde4b6]…\nmake fpga TARGET=bench`: PASS for all three Gowin placements.\\n\\n## Measured fitness\\n\\n- Placement Fmax: 54.304, 55.226, 55.226 MHz; median **55.226 MHz**.\\n- Unchanged stalled, CRC-validated, marker-bracketed CoreMark: **4,478,376\\n  cycles**, 10 iterations, 0.00000223295230235246 iterations/cycle.\\n- Compared with 4,197,447 baseline cycles: +280,929 cycles, **+6.69285%**.\\n- Fitness: **123.32 iterations/second**, **+5.06%** over 117.38.\\n- Clears the required **122.78** threshold by **0.54**.\\n- Placement-0 resources: 3651 logic, 1095 registers, 40 LUT-RAM,\\n  7 BSRAM, 2 DSP.\\n\\nThe acceptance margin is small; this achieves the required fitness margin\\nbut not the hypothesized 20% improvement. Predictor/recovery logic remains\\nthe measured timing limit and was intentionally preserved. Full real\\narithmetic `formal-deep` was not run; real arithmetic was exercised by the\\nexpanded unit vectors and unchanged retirement/CRC cosim gates.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T01:19:43.775245Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 3}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
