ed to be \"$CORE_NAME-$$\", but an\n# agent's sandboxed shell runs in its own PID namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n# for every agent, so siblings wrote into one dir and wiped each other's\n# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n# FORMAL_WORK_ID pins the suffix so tools/eval/formal.py can remove exactly\n# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core\n…[7299 of 10371 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:67ef104a4c28dfc4]…\nsim/main.cpp:32:// Benchmark-time MMIO markers. CoreMark's portme.c writes to BENCH_START\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:35:// bench_cycles = stop - start, excluding init/CRC-printing overhead.\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:70:    //           (tools/eval/fpga.py:run_coremark_ipc) passes BOTH so the\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:111:    uint64_t bench_start_cycle = 0, bench_stop_cycle = 0;\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:131:        //     allowed (markers); anything else outside dmem is OOB (handled\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:152:            // BENCH_START/BENCH_STOP markers at 0x10000100 / 0x10000104: record\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:157:                if (!bench_start_set) { bench_start_cycle = cycle; bench_start_set = true; }\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:161:                bench_stop_cycle = cycle; bench_stop_set = true;\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:268:               \"\\\"bench_start_cycle\\\":%llu,\\\"bench_stop_cycle\\\":%llu,\"\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:273:               (unsigned long long)bench_start_cycle,\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:274:               (unsigned long long)bench_stop_cycle,\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
