{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"The extra result stage raises Fmax but adds about 20% to CoreMark cycles, so it loses overall. The final candidate moves general ALU operand selection before the existing EX registers, extending the approach that improved the multiplier. It preserves instruction latency and avoids the dependency cost of another stage."}}
