tor-update cones may still cap Fmax.\n\nValidate unchanged legality, arithmetic and retirement-cosim gates, plus\npipeline tests for paired saved controls/immediates, consume/refill,\nfull/empty holds, buffered decode with imemReady low, load-use, division,\nboth buses stalled, reset and wrong-path store/divider squashing. Run the\nunchanged nret=1 formal checks. Score canonical CRC-validated stalled\nCoreMark bracket cycles times median Gowin Fmax. Acceptance requires more\nthan 193.42 iter/sec; timing or area improvement alone is insufficient.\n'''\nh['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nh['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Extend the accepted fetch bundle with decoded ctrl_t and immediate; add general alu_a/alu_b words to ID/EX alongside finalized raw operands and multiplier sign bits. Keep all metadata paired through stalls, reset and flush.'},\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Instantiate the unchanged decoder and immediate generator before a one-entry elastic registered fetch/decode transaction. Implement readiness-qualified fill, genuine head consumption, simultaneous replacement, full-slot hold and redirect-priority discard. Advance PC only on accepted fill or recovery, with no combinational decode bypass.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Consume saved controls and immediate instead of decoding live imem data. Read source addresses from the saved instruction, retain youngest-producer forwarding, and capture finalized raw operands plus PC/rs1-selected ALU A and immediate/rs2-selected ALU B on the existing ID/EX acceptance edge.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Drive ordinary ALU a/b directly from the prepared ID/EX words, removing late AUIPC and immediate operand muxes. Retain raw branch/store/RVFI sources, native multiplier formatting, division handshake, immediate accepted recovery and predictor training.'},\n {'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'Separate fetch-bus availability from consumption of the decoded head. Preserve load-use bubbles, division and data-memory holds; a missing new fetch cannot invalidate buffered work and a bubble cannot pop it. Keep existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB acceptance rules.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire registered decoded-head validity, imemReady and actual operand-stage consumption to the elastic frontend. Drive source checks and forwarding from the saved transaction; retain the exact nret=1 ports, predictor policy, arithmetic and retirement logic.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve architectural assertions while adapting fetch-acceptance observations to the elastic slot. Cover controls/immediates paired with PC/instruction, back-to-back consume/refill, buffered progress during imem stalls, full/empty holds, all producer stages and ALU operand kinds, division, both bus stalls, recovery and reset. Require exact RVFI values/order, stable held requests and once-only memory effects.'}\n]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote refined, schema-valid structural hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Wrote refined, schema-valid structural hypothesis: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r6s1.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
