{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261005-003-r5s2','hyp-20261005-001-r6s0','hyp-20261005-001-r7s0']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261005-003-r5s2 Train the predictor from registered EX/MEM control-flow results\nMove only the predictor-training boundary from combinational EX acceptance\nto consumption of the existing registered EX/MEM instruction in MEM.\nKeep the exact 64-entry direct-mapped predictor, all tag/target/counter\nwidths, PC-only lookup, bimodal direction policy, jump behavior, range and\nalignment guards, and old-row lookup timing. Do not change instruction\npipeline depth, operand forwarding, arithmetic, fetch acceptance or the\nEX misprediction-recovery boundary. This is one predictor feedback-pipeline\nexperiment; no capacity, banking, history or metadata redesign is included.\n\nDrive predictor_update_en from ex_mem_w.valid && !hold_mem_wb && !reset.\nThis consumes one registered instruction exactly once: a true data-memory\nhold suppresses training until MEM accepts, and the existing EX/MEM hold\nor bubble behavior prevents repeats after consumption. Derive update_pc\nfrom ex_mem_w.pc, branch/jump kind from its registered controls and legal\nfrom !ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_illegal. Derive actual taken as legal AND\n(ex_mem_w.branch_taken OR ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_jump). For jumps, update_target\nis ex_mem_w.pc_next, the registered architectural jump destination; for\nconditional branches it is ex_mem_w.branch_target, including the direct\ntarget on a not-taken outcome. Never substitute PC+4 for a not-taken branch\ntraining target. On illegal or misaligned control transfers the registered\ntrap control marks the update illegal, so the unchanged predictor performs\nmatching-only invalidation instead of allocation. Non-control instructions\nstill provide registered stale-entry invalidation opportunities.\n\nRemove the seven combinational predictor_update outputs and assignments\nfrom ex_stage and derive them centrally from EX/MEM in core. Keep the\nexisting branch_taken, branch_target, pc_next, PC and effective controls\nregistered in ex_stage; these fields already contain the required results.\nDo not forward current EX values around this boundary and do not add\n…[10357 of 13429 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9c91020a5996a6f0]…\n and routing paths may limit the\nbenefit. At unchanged cycles, median Fmax must exceed about 85.29 MHz.\nDo not present a single-placement result as a scored median.\n\nPreserve every current architectural behavior: EX/MEM/WB forwarding and\npriority, captured source/RVFI values, JAL/JALR links, AUIPC and full-width\naddresses, balanced branch comparisons, direction/target recovery,\npredictor policy/training, illegal and misalignment traps, memory\nbackpressure and nret=1 IO/retirement. Keep all existing assertions and\nchecks, including zero bubbles and full-bundle stability under holds.\nVerify all fourteen groups, all M-extension variants, youngest-writer\nsources, x0, load dependencies and reset/recovery during stalled execution.\nRun real arithmetic vectors, strict real/ALTOPS lint, unchanged formal and\nretirement cosim, then canonical stalled CoreMark with exact CRC/UART,\nbounds and marker-bracketed cycles. Score actual median Gowin Fmax times\nmeasured iterations/cycle; modify only allowed RTL and cocotb tests.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/generated/r8s1_probe; cat > cores/bench/generated/r8s1_probe/prepare.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nbase=Path('cores/bench/generated/r8s1_probe')\nrtl=base/'rtl'\nrtl.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nfor p in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'): shutil.copy2(p,rtl/p.name)\np=rtl/'core_pkg.sv';s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('    logic        branch_taken;','    logic        recover;\\\\n    logic        branch_taken;');p.write_text(s)\np=rtl/'ex_stage.sv';s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('  input  id_ex_t   in,','  input  logic               squash,\\\\n  input  id_ex_t   in,')\nstart=s.index('  output logic               div_wait,');end=s.index('\\\\n);',start)\ns=s[:start]+'  output logic               div_wait'+s[end:]\ns=s.replace('\"'!stall && !reset;'\"', '\"'!stall && !squash && !reset;'\"')\ns=s.replace('assign div_wait = is_div && \"'!div_consume;'\"', 'assign div_wait = is_div && \"'!div_consume && !squash;'\"')\ns=s.replace('  logic ex_accept, actual_taken, direction_mismatch, target_mismatch;', '  logic actual_taken, direction_mismatch, target_mismatch;')\ns=s.replace('  assign ex_accept = in.valid && \"'!stall && !div_wait && !reset;'\"\\\\n','')\nstart=s.index('  assign redirect = ');end=s.index('  // ── EX/MEM register',start)\ns=s[:start]+s[end:]\ns=s.replace('    if (reset) begin\\\\n      reg_q', '    if (reset || squash) begin\\\\n      reg_q')\ns=s.replace('      reg_q.branch_taken  <= branch_taken;', '      reg_q.recover       <= direction_mismatch || target_mismatch;\\\\n      reg_q.branch_taken  <= branch_taken;')\np.write_text(s)\np=rtl/'core.sv';s=p.read_text();start=s.index('    .div_wait        (div_wait),');end=s.index('\\\\n  );',start)\ns=s[:start]+'    .div_wait        (div_wait),\\\\n    .squash          (redirect)'+s[end:]\nanchor='  // ── RVFI '\nstart=s.index(anchor)\nnew='''  // Registered MEM-stage control-flo