{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nb=Path('cores/bench/generated/r8s1_completion').resolve();f=b/'formal';f.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nshutil.copy2('formal/run_all.sh',f/'run_all.sh');r=f/'riscv-formal';r.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nfor name in ['checks','insns']:shutil.copytree(Path('formal/riscv-formal')/name,r/name,dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=b/'.toolchain'\nif not p.exists():p.symlink_to(Path('.toolchain').resolve(),target_is_directory=True)\nPY\nRTL_DIR=rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 WRAPPER=\\\"\"'$PWD/formal/wrapper_si.sv\" CHECKS_CFG=\"$PWD/formal/checks_si.cfg\" bash cores/bench/generated/r8s1_completion/formal/run_all.sh > cores/bench/generated/r8s1_completion/formal.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r8s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Make EX/MEM the sole result and control-flow completion boundary'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 canonical\nstalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Read structural\nattempts r2s1, r4s1, r5s1, r6s1 and r7s1 and predictor attempt r5s2.\nThe successful finalized-ID-operand boundary still leaves two live EX\nfeedback routes: result forwarding into ID and recovery/training through\nthe predictor and front end. Delaying only control feedback leaves ALU\nforwarding critical; removing only EX forwarding leaves predictor feedback\ncritical. One coherent completion boundary must cut both outgoing routes\nbefore either can dominate the clock.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Use the existing EX/MEM register as the sole completion boundary for\nboth architectural producer data and control-flow feedback. EX computes\narithmetic, branch comparisons, full targets, traps and prediction\nmismatches from the current finalized ID/EX flops. Those results advance\ninto EX/MEM before they can feed younger operand capture, fetch recovery\nor predictor training. Retain current ordinary stage count and one issue\nper cycle for independent instructions. This is one structural execution\ncompletion partition; it changes dependency scheduling and recovery\nlatency rather than predictor policy or arithmetic implementation.\n\nRemove the combinational current-EX result bypass into ID, including its\nforwarding tag/priority path and its operand-data input. ID selects only\nthe current registered EX/MEM producer in MEM, including sign/zero-extended\nloads, then RF with the existing WB write-first bypass. Keep x0 priority,\neffective nontrapping producer qualification and exact raw RVFI sources.\nA valid ID/EX register writer with a nonzero destination is pending for\nits immediately younger matching encoded source fields. Generalize the\nexisting load-use interlock to all such unavailable EX results: hold PC,\nbubble ID/EX once when EX can advance, and capture the registered MEM\nresult on the following acceptance edge. Keep the existing raw source\nmatching convention, including unused encoded fields, so captured RVFI\nsource values remain consistent. Do not add a bubble for an independent\ninstruction or a writer to x0. A genuine dmem hold or pending division\nholds ID/EX instead of clearing the producer; re-evaluate readiness when\nit can advance. Completed division also reaches consumers through MEM.\n\nCapture one prediction-recovery bit in EX/MEM with the existing resolved\npc_next and instruction metadata. Derive redirect only from valid saved\nrecovery on actual EX/MEM consumption, never from live EX arithmetic or\ncomparison. Derive every predictor-training field from the same registered\ninstruction: PC, effective legality and branch/jump type, actual taken,\nand actual target. Reuse existing registered pc_next for jump destinations\nand branch_target for conditional branches, including not-taken training.\nKeep the exact 64-entry tagged predictor, absolute targets, counters,\nrange/alignment guards, old-row lookup/update behavior, weak replacement\ninitialization and matching-only stale invalidation. Ordinary/illegal\ninstructions retain once-per-consumption stale-entry invalidation.\n\nOn saved recovery redirect the fetch PC, clear ID/EX, and clear the younger\nprospective EX/MEM transfer completely. The older resolving instruction\nstill advances into MEM/WB, trains once and retires once with its exact\nPC, next PC, sources and JAL/JALR link. Correct predictions do not flush.\nHandle direction errors, taken target errors, stale ordinary predictions\nand changing JALR targets. Trapping transfers retain suppressed writes\nand PC+4 recovery semantics. Recovery takes priority over younger source\ninterlocks, imem unavailability and division holds. Gate divider start\nand consume on absence of recovery so a squashed younger division cannot\nlaunch an orphan request. Preserve a genuine unaccepted older memory\nrequest: saved recovery/training waits for its MEM consumption. Raw low\ndmemReady does not hold a non-memory completion. Bubble/hold/reset rules\nmust prevent repeated recovery, training, retirement or memory effects.\n\nPreserve finalized ID/EX operand and multiplier-sign flops, the shared\nnative multiplier, sticky iterative divider, older-stage draining, load\nextraction, full-width PC/address arithmetic, real RV32IM results and exact\nALTOPS formulas. Retain nret=1 and the exact memory/RVFI ports, strict order,\ndecoder legality defaults, all existing trap behavior, memory bounds,\ncanonical CRCs, timing markers and every unchanged correctness contract.\nModify only allowed RTL and cocotb tests. Do not change wrappers, harness,\nformal settings/depth, benchmark sources or evaluation methodology.\n\nTwo isolated diagnostic prototypes pass all eight stalled/zero-wait\nretirement cosims and canonical CoreMark CRC/completion/bounds/bracketing\nvalidation. Registering control feedback alone gives 4259763 cycles and\n80.654 MHz median Gowin Fmax; disabling EX result forwarding alone gives\n4709754 cycles and 81.839 MHz. The second prototype passes all 53 unchanged\nnret=1 fast formal checks. Neither is a proposed winning candidate. These\nmeasurements identify independent timing limits and justify cutting both\nroutes together. The combined topology remains under investigation.\n\nPredict an eight percent fitness gain with low confidence, pending the\ncombined vendor result. Extra adjacent RAW bubbles and one extra recovery\nslot per miss are the explicit throughput costs. A roughly 14 percent\ncycle increase needs about 97.3 MHz median Fmax to clear the 4.6 percent\nacceptance margin. Residual RF access, memory extraction or intrinsic EX\narithmetic may prevent that gain. Acceptance requires actual canonical\nstalled marker-bracketed iterations/cycle times fresh median Gowin Fmax\nabove 203.1855 iter/sec; a timing-only gain is insufficient.'''\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add a saved recovery bit to ex_mem_t. Reuse existing full-width PC, pc_next, branch_target, branch_taken and effective controls for registered completion and training. Keep every architectural/RVFI payload field.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Remove live EX producer routing to ID. Connect only MEM producer and WB-bypassed RF sources. Generalize unavailable-result interlocking and derive recovery/training exclusively from consumed EX/MEM fields. Route saved recovery to younger EX squash, IF and ID while preserving older MEM/WB advancement and exact nret=1 IO/RVFI.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Keep arithmetic launched from finalized operand flops and capture results plus prediction-recovery bit at EX/MEM. Replace live recovery/training outputs with registered completion. Add saved-recovery squash, suppress wrong-path divider launch/consume and clear the younger EX/MEM transfer. Preserve once-only division, effective traps, PC/link/source values and older draining.'},\n {'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'Generalize the load-use interlock to any unavailable current-EX register result with valid effective write and nonzero destination. Preserve raw encoded-source matching. On a matching consumer hold PC and bubble ID/EX only when the producer advances; dmem/division holds retain it. Recovery overrides younger interlocks. Existing load-use latency stays one bubble; independent instructions retain full throughput.'},\n {'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Remove current-EX producer matching and priority. Select valid nontrapping current-MEM results before WB-bypassed RF for each source; x0 never matches. No live EX arithmetic result may reach the ID operand capture path.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Remove the live EX result input/selection and capture finalized operands from MEM or WB-bypassed RF on genuine acceptance. Keep decoder legality, multiplier-sign preparation, full metadata clearing and complete stable holds.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve every architectural, trap, RVFI source/result/PC/order and once-only-memory assertion. Adapt only throughput and feedback-stage scheduling assertions to registered completion: one RAW bubble for all unavailable results, no independent-instruction bubble, and training once per MEM consumption. Add all producer classes, competing writers, x0, load/division interactions, changing/stale predictions, wrong-path store/load/jump/division squash, both bus stalls and reset. Require unchanged lint, arithmetic/decoder tests, all formal checks, retirement cosim and canonical CRC-valid CoreMark before fresh vendor scoring.'}\n]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef rep(dumper,s):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised single structural hypothesis: schema PASS')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
