{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"The payload-retention prototype passes all eight retirement cosims. It keeps the current forwarding and recovery latency, and explicitly qualifies memory requests and load hazards with stage validity. The remaining question is whether reducing wide bubble-clear control produces enough timing gain."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r8s1.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Separate pipeline validity from retained instruction payloads'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 canonical\nstalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Structural history\nincludes successful finalized ID operands, unsuccessful extra decode and\nmultiply stages, and a banked register file below the acceptance margin.\nThe current front end inserts a NOP through an imemReady-controlled\ninstruction mux, while ID/EX and EX/MEM synchronously zero entire wide\npayloads for bubbles or flushes. Those controls reach source-address,\noperand-capture and DSP input-register paths. Retaining invalid payloads\ncan simplify the physical control network without extra dependency or\nrecovery cycles, unlike moving completion later.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Partition each existing pipeline register into an instruction-valid bit\nand retained payload. An invalid bubble must clear validity instead of\nzeroing every operand, immediate, control and metadata bit. Payload is\nwritten only on genuine instruction acceptance and otherwise remains\nstable through bubbles, flushes and holds. Keep synchronous reset clearing\nthe whole bundle to zero, preserving deterministic reset-visible fields.\nThis is one structural change to pipeline storage and side-effect\nqualification, with no new stage, scheduling policy or instruction latency.\n\nIn IF, present raw imemData as the combinational instruction payload even\nwhen imemReady is low; use out.valid to represent availability rather than\nsubstituting a NOP before decoder and RF source-address extraction. Keep\nexisting accepted prediction metadata, PC advancement, imem stalls and\nredirect priority. Unavailable raw data can be arbitrary: ID must never\naccept it as a valid instruction or launch a side effect from it.\n\nIn ID/EX, reset still clears the complete bundle. A redirect flush,\nload-use bubble or accepted unavailable fetch clears only reg_q.valid.\nEvery payload field retains its previous value. An ordinary hold retains\nboth validity and payload; genuine accepted valid instructions replace\nthe complete paired payload and set validity. Preserve flush priority over\nhold, finalized youngest EX > MEM > RF operands, WB write-first behavior,\nmultiplier-sign preparation and strict decoder/default-illegal logic.\nDo not recapture held operands while older stages drain.\n\nIn EX/MEM, reset still clears the complete bundle. Genuine dmem backpressure\nholds the full register. When the previous MEM instruction is consumed and\nEX supplies no valid instruction or is waiting for division, clear only\nEX/MEM validity and retain payload. A real accepted EX instruction replaces\nall payload fields and sets validity. MEM/WB already clears only validity\nunder dmem hold; retain its current retirement/writeback discipline.\n\nBecause invalid controls now retain old values, make validity authoritative\nat every active use. Qualify the EX load-use predicate with ID/EX.valid and\nqualify the dmem-hold memory-op predicate with EX/MEM.valid. In MEM, read\nenable and every store write-enable bit require EX/MEM.valid in addition\nto the existing access control and alignment conditions. An invalid saved\nload must not stall fetch or assert dmemREn; an invalid saved store must\nnot assert any byte write-enable. Audit forwarding, WB writes, divider\nstart/consume/wait, predictor training, recovery and retirement: each must\nalready require or explicitly acquire the owning stage's validity. Invalid\npayload must never produce an architectural register write, memory effect,\npredictor update, redirect, divider launch or retirement. Retaining data\nis permitted only because those effects are independently suppressed.\n\nPreserve current true operand-launch flops and all accepted-instruction\nlatencies, the exact 64-entry predictor and same-cycle EX recovery,\nfull-width address/PC arithmetic, balanced branch comparison, native\nmultiplier, sticky iterative divider, older-stage draining and all real\nRV32IM/ALTOPS behavior. Keep nret=1 and exact top-level memory/RVFI ports,\nconsecutive retirement order, legality/traps, bounds, canonical CRCs and\nmarkers. All top-level fields stay driven and reset-defined. Do not modify\nwrappers, formal depth/properties, benchmarks, harness or evaluation.\n\nThe intended gain comes from removing ready-dependent instruction masking\nand wide bubble/flush zero muxes ahead of operand/DSP capture, and reducing\ncontrol fanout through retained payload registers. It should incur no\nCoreMark cycle cost. This is a prediction pending vendor results. Estimate\nan eight percent gain with low confidence: synchronous reset, payload\nclock enables or existing arithmetic/predictor feedback can still dominate.\nAt unchanged cycles the median vendor Fmax must exceed approximately\n85.286 MHz and fitness must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec to clear acceptance.\nMeasure actual CRC-valid stalled marker-bracketed cycles and median Gowin\ntiming rather than inferring fitness from register count or one placement.\n\nAn isolated prototype has passed strict real-arithmetic lint and all eight\nunchanged retirement comparisons for selftest and random1/2/3, each with\nand without both memory stalls. Final implementation must pass unchanged\narithmetic/decoder tests, every formal check, pipeline architecture tests,\ncanonical CoreMark validation and fresh median vendor scoring. Update only\ninternal bubble-representation assertions from whole-bundle-zero to valid\nclear plus absence of every side effect; retain all architectural result,\nsource, PC, trap, order, progress and memory assertions.'''\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Remove the unavailable-fetch NOP substitution from the instruction data path. Present raw imemData and preserve availability through valid. Keep PC/ready/redirect acceptance and paired predictor metadata unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Split invalidation from payload update: reset clears the full ID/EX bundle; flush or unavailable/bubbled input clears only validity; holds preserve the whole bundle; valid acceptance captures complete finalized operands, controls, immediate, instruction and prediction metadata. Preserve every forwarding and decoder rule.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'On a consumed EX/MEM entry followed by division wait or invalid EX input, clear only EX/MEM validity and retain payload. Keep reset full-clear, genuine memory holds, valid complete writes, same-cycle branch recovery, arithmetic and sticky division. Audit all EX effect enables for owning validity.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Qualify load-use input with ID/EX.valid and the memory-hold predicate with EX/MEM.valid so retained invalid control bits cannot block progress. Audit validity qualification of forwarding, retirement, WB, predictor and recovery. Preserve all top-level nret=1 ports and RVFI metadata.'},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Require EX/MEM.valid for dmemREn and every dmemWEn bit in addition to existing decoded access and alignment conditions. Preserve valid load extraction, store replication/masks, producer forwarding, MEM/WB validity handling and architectural/RVFI results.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all architectural/source/result/PC/order/trap/progress/memory assertions. Replace only the internal all-zero-bundle bubble assertion with validity-clear plus explicit no-side-effect checks. Add valid store/load followed by imem bubbles, divider bubbles, load-use and redirect flushes while retained controls remain nonzero; poison unavailable imem data; test reset and combined holds. Assert no invalid memory requests, false load stalls, writes, updates, redirects, divider launch or retirement, stable retained payload and unchanged valid instruction latency. Run unchanged lint/formal/arithmetic/decoder/cosim and canonical CoreMark gates before median vendor scoring.'}\n]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dm,s:dm.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Complete validity/payload structural hypothesis: schema PASS')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
