{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r8s1.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Decouple speculative operand capture from instruction kill control'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 canonical\nstalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Reviewed structural\nhistory includes successful finalized ID operands, unsuccessful extra\ndecode/multiply stages and insufficient banked-RF gains. Recent timing\npaths reach the finalized operand/DSP registers through EX recovery,\npredictor and front-end controls. ID currently clears its entire payload\non flush or unavailable fetch, and IF substitutes NOP before decoding\nunavailable data. These mechanisms couple instruction kill/availability\nto operand capture even though invalid instructions cannot execute.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Split the existing ID/EX register's update protocol into speculative\npayload capture and architectural control acceptance. Whenever \"'!stall,\ncapture PC, instruction, prediction metadata, finalized raw rs1/rs2,\nmultiplier extension bits, immediate and source/destination addresses,\nregardless of flush or in.valid. Separately preserve the existing\nvalid/control protocol: reset clears the whole bundle; flush or an\nunavailable nonheld input clears valid and ctrl; an ordinary nonheld\nvalid input captures decoded ctrl and sets valid; genuine hold retains\nboth payload and control. Give flush priority over hold for valid/ctrl.\nUse one always_ff or disjoint field ownership without multiple drivers.\nThe payload enable must not depend on redirect/flush or fetch validity.\nThis is one structural partition of speculative data registers from\ninstruction acceptance, with no added stage, dependency bubble or latency.\n\nPresent raw imemData from IF instead of replacing an unavailable fetch\nwith NOP. out.valid still represents imemReady availability through the\nexisting flush input. Preserve fetch PC advancement, accepted prediction\nmetadata, front-end holds and recovery priority exactly. Decode and RF\naccess may process unavailable or wrong-path words speculatively, but\nthe corresponding ID/EX valid and every ctrl field are cleared, so that\ndata cannot execute or retire. Keep the decoder'\"'s default-illegal and\npositive opcode/funct validation unchanged; do not make missing data a\nlegal instruction or use it to advance PC.\n\nRetain clearing all control fields on bubbles/flushes. In particular,\nmem_read, mem_write, reg_write and branch/jump controls stay zero when\ninvalid. This keeps the current load-use, memory-hold and side-effect\nlogic safe without adding new valid gates to timed memory predicates.\nKeep full EX/MEM bubble clearing, current MEM/WB validity discipline,\nproducer validity qualifications, WB write gating, divider valid launch\nand EX-accept-qualified predictor training/recovery. The only invalid\nstate that changes representation is ID/EX payload, which may now contain\nspeculative data while valid and controls are zero. Reset still clears\nall payload/control fields, keeping all external fields driven and defined.\n\nPreserve finalized youngest EX > MEM > RF forwarding and WB write-first\nbypass on every valid acceptance edge. Preserve x0, paired raw RVFI sources,\nregistered multiplier sign bits and exact full-payload stability under\ntrue ID/EX holds. A flush concurrent with hold clears only validity/control\nand retains held data. Never refresh a valid held division's operands as\nolder stages drain. Architectural retirement, memory effects, branch/PC\nbehavior, dependency latency and stall sequencing must remain unchanged.\n\nKeep nret=1 and the exact IO/RVFI shape, the current 64-entry predictor,\nbalanced comparator, native multiplier, sticky iterative divider, every\nreal RV32IM result and exact ALTOPS formula, trap/legality behavior,\nstrict order, progress, bounds, CRCs and markers. Modify only allowed\nRTL and cocotb tests. Do not change any wrapper, formal property/depth,\nbenchmark, harness or scoring contract.\n\nPredict a six percent fitness gain with low confidence before final timing.\nThe intended gain is removing kill/availability from payload register\nclear/enables and removing the instruction-mask mux before source access.\nThe ordinary arithmetic, forwarding or retained control-register paths\nmay still dominate, so this is not a demonstrated champion replacement.\nAt unchanged cycles median Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 85.286 MHz\nand fitness must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec to clear the 4.6 percent gate.\nUse actual canonical stalled marker-bracketed cycles and fresh median\nvendor Fmax, never a circuit-neutral placement gain or RVFI-only change.\n\nAn isolated implementation has passed strict real-arithmetic lint and\nall eight unchanged full-retirement cosims (selftest and random1/2/3,\neach zero-wait and with both stalls). Final implementation must complete\nunchanged arithmetic/decoder/formal tests, pipeline architectural tests,\ncanonical CoreMark validation and fresh median vendor scoring. Update only\nthe internal whole-bundle-zero flush assertion to require valid=0 and\nctrl=0 with absence of every side effect; retain every architectural\nsource/result/PC/trap/order/progress and memory assertion.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Present raw imemData without unavailable-fetch NOP substitution. Keep valid, PC/ready/redirect acceptance and paired prediction metadata semantics unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Separate speculative payload writes under \"'!stall from valid/ctrl updates. Reset fully clears; flush/unavailable input clears valid and all ctrl fields; ordinary acceptance captures controls; true hold retains data. Payload capture ignores flush and input validity, while all control priority and finalized forwarding/sign preparation remain unchanged.'\"'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all functional and latency assertions. Replace only internal whole-bundle-zero invalidation expectations with valid=0, ctrl=0 and explicit absence of effects. Add poisoned unavailable imem data and wrong-path payload capture across redirects, load-use and both bus holds; verify valid held operands stay stable, no invalid divider/predictor/memory/register/retirement effect, exact RVFI/order, reset-defined outputs and unchanged valid latency. Run unchanged arithmetic/decoder/lint/formal/cosim and canonical CoreMark validation before median vendor scoring.'}\n]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dm,s:dm.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final operand/control partition proposal: schema PASS')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
