h prediction: every aligned taken branch, JAL,\\nor JALR redirects from EX and discards the younger fetched instruction.\\nIF/ID is combinational rather than registered, so the fetched instruction\\nis already available early enough to decode direct control-flow targets\\nand choose the next fetch PC. CoreMark's repeated loops should benefit\\nfrom avoiding these\n…[262821 of 265893 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f9e5a5b71ecc6c53]…\n; exercise short loops, consecutive control flow, stale code,\\ntarget changes and reset under delayed training. Require independent\\nimmediate recovery and exact retirement/order/link/source behavior\\nunder all original stalls, with no wrong-path memory side effects.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 196.33, \"delta_pct\": 1.07, \"vs_baseline\": 1519.88, \"fmax_mhz\": 82.407, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4197447, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4500, \"ff\": 1897, \"seeds\": [80.132, 82.407, 82.407], \"perturbations\": [[0, 80.132, 11], [1, 82.407, 11], [2, 82.407, 11]], \"lutram\": 32, \"bsram\": 5, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_30_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_product_65_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -7.479, \"arrival_ns\": 17.553, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T05:36:00.210204Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
