{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|return.address|return stack|gshare|BTB|alias|branch prediction' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Small bimodal predictor with targets decoded directly at fetch\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline has no branch prediction: every aligned taken branch, JAL,\\nor JALR redirects from EX and discards the younger fetched instruction.\\nIF/ID is combinational rather than registered, so the fetched instruction\\nis already available early enough to decode direct control-flow targets\\nand choose the next fetch PC. CoreMark's repeated loops should benefit\\nfrom avoiding these one-cycle bubbles. A small direction-only table avoids\\nthe area and wide read muxes of a tagged branch-target buffer. The measured\\ncritical path passes through forwarding and the combinational M-extension\\nALU, so a modest predictor is unlikely to become the limiting timing path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline has no branch prediction: every aligned taken branch, JAL,\\nor JALR redirects from EX and discards the younger fetched instruction.\\nIF/ID is combinational rather than registered, so the fetched instruction\\nis already available early enough to decode direct control-flow targets\\nand choose the next fetch PC. CoreMark's repeated loops should benefit\\nfrom avoiding these one-cycle bubbles. A small direction-only table avoids\\nthe area and wide read muxes of a tagged branch-target buffer. The measured\\ncritical path passes through forwarding and the combinational M-extension\\nALU, so a modest predictor is unlikely to become the limiting timing path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one fetch-stage bimodal predictor: 128 two-bit saturating counters,\\nindexed by PC[8:2] and reset to weakly not taken. Decode the raw fetched\\ninstruction to recognize legal conditional branch funct3 values and JAL.\\nFor a conditional branch, predict taken when its indexed counter's MSB is\\nset; predict JAL taken unconditionally. Construct B/J immediates directly\\nfrom the instruction and add them to the current fetch PC. Predict only\\nword-aligned targets; use PC+4 for all other instructions, inclu\n…[303018 of 306090 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3d471c9aa6782192]…\n / 77.674 | 77.674 | 185.05 |\\n| Factored tag matching and Boolean saturation, reverted | 70.811 / 75.428 / 75.428 | 75.428 | 179.70 |\\n\\nThe retained implementation uses 4,789 Gowin logic cells, 1,938 registers,\\n52 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its reported critical path has eleven logic\\nlevels and crosses EX/ID operand/result selection into the multiplier input\\nregister. Repeating the full FPGA fitness measurement after restoration reproduced\\nall three placement frequencies, the 4,197,447-cycle count and 185.05 fitness.\\n\\nThe hypothesis does not meet the required fitness threshold of 203.1855\\niterations/sec: the retained measurement is 185.05058 iterations/sec. At the measured\\ncycle count it would need more than 85.28604 MHz median Fmax. No acceptance win or\\nestimated six-percent gain is claimed. Additional training latency and residual\\nEX/ID paths prevent this measured implementation from establishing an improvement.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T06:18:32.465461Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
