B/J immediates directly\nfrom the instruction and add them to the current fetch PC. Predict only\nword-aligned targets; use PC+4 for all other instructions, including JALR,\nreserved branch encodings, and misaligned direct targets. Do not add a BTB,\nreturn-address stack, global history, cache, or arithmetic redesign.\n\nCarry the exact predicted next PC with each accepted instruction through\nIF/ID and ID/EX. Advance the PC to that prediction only when the existing\nfetch/decode handshake accepts the instruction. Prediction must not advance\nthe PC during imem backpressure, load-use interlocks, or dmem backpressure.\nIn EX retain the existing forwarded operands, branch comparison, target\ncalculation, jump link value, and misalignment/trap b\n…[57229 of 60301 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:79854992aa3c24cb]…\nt indirect prediction can erase savings;\nresidual ALU/ID forwarding remains a limit. A direction-table prototype\nwith a separate validity bitmap and full 32-bit target adder measured\nonly 76.011 MHz median and therefore does not establish a win. Local\ndirection flops, saved-lookup maintenance and counter re-encoding also\nregressed in exploratory checks and are excluded. The final proposal\nspecifically removes the redundant direction-valid state and bounds\nthe prediction sum to 22 bits; do not claim measured acceptance.\n\nScore actual canonical marker-bracketed CoreMark iterations/cycle times\nmedian Gowin Fmax. Require fitness above 203.1855 iter/sec to clear the\n4.6 percent threshold, and require all unchanged unit/formal/cosim gates,\nCRCs, bounds, completion text and both timing markers. Preserve nret=1\nand top-level IO, decoder default illegality, RVFI PC/link/operands/order,\nprogress, true/ALTOPS arithmetic, memory handshakes and every hard\ninvariant. Modify only the listed allowed RTL and tests.\n\n notes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
