\ntraining target. On illegal or misaligned control transfers the registered\ntrap control marks the update illegal, so the unchanged predictor performs\nmatching-only invalidation instead of allocation. Non-control instructions\nstill provide registered stale-entry invalidation opportunities.\n\nRemove the seven combinational predictor_update outputs and assignments\nfrom ex_stage and derive them centrally from EX/MEM in core. Keep the\nexisting branch_taken, branch_target, pc_next, PC and effective controls\nregistered in ex_stage; these fields already contain the required results.\nDo not forward current EX values around this\n…[20426 of 23498 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6b839579dcc0647c]…\ns all canonical CRCs and completion text,\nand the run completes at EBREAK, in bounds, with both markers. Verilator\nlint passes. All eight retirement cosim comparisons pass for selftest\nand random1/random2/random3, each under zero-wait and imem+dmem stalls.\nThe unchanged formal suite and unit tests remain implementation gates;\nno formal pass is claimed for this isolated hypothesis prototype.\n\nAt 4197447 cycles the selected prototype yields 197.7107 iter/sec,\napproximately 1.78 percent above 194.25. This is below the required\n203.1855 acceptance score; do not claim it clears the 4.6 percent margin.\nExpected integer fitness gain is 2 percent with medium confidence.\nRecheck exact canonical stalled CoreMark cycles, CRCs, completion,\nbounds and bracketing, all original tests and formal/cosim gates, and\nactual median Gowin timing on the implementation. Remaining uncertainty\nis correctness coverage and the unchanged IF/ID and ALU forwarding paths,\nwhich limit the gain after predictor feedback is registered.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
