{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r13s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Separate bimodal direction history from tagged target maintenance\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 64-entry predictor couples two-bit direction updates to\n  an update-addressed tag comparison, validity selection and jump-kind\n  read. Its EX-to-predictor maintenance cone appears in recent critical\n  paths. Previous banking, delayed training, fetch-target arithmetic and\n  fetch-captured maintenance experiments regressed; LESSONS.md is absent.\n  Keep the successful PC-only stored-target lookup, but separate direction\n  history so its counter update no longer waits for a BTB tag/kind match.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the existing predictor into the unchanged 64-entry tagged target\n  buffer and an independent 128-entry untagged bimodal direction table.\n  The target buffer retains PC[7:2] indexing, PC[19:8] tags, eighteen-bit\n  target words, unconditional-jump kind and reset-only validity. Remove\n  counter_q from its rows. The direction table is indexed by PC[8:2] and\n  stores one ordinary two-bit saturating counter per row plus a separately\n  reset direction-valid bitmap. Leave counter payload unreset, using 01\n  as the effective counter when direction-valid is zero. Use native arrays\n  with asynchronous fetch/update reads and one synchronous write port;\n  do not add banks, per-row replicated training logic or another stage.\n\n  A full guarded BTB tag hit is still required for any taken prediction.\n  Jump hits predict taken unconditionally and ignore the direction table.\n  Conditional hits use the effective direction counter's MSB. A miss,\n  invalid or unrepresentable lookup predicts not taken with zero target.\n  A valid hit exposes its original stored target even when not taken.\n  Fetch lookup remains a function of registered PC and predictor storage;\n  it does not inspect instruction-memory data or compute a target adder.\n\n  On each original EX-accepted, legal conditional-branch update with an\n  in-range aligned PC and representable aligned direct target, saturate\n  on\n…[2993 of 6065 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3ba48972868eeba3]…\n: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt direction-policy checks to an independent bimodal reference\n      model while retaining target/tag/jump/reset/guard assertions. Cover\n      all 128 direction rows, every saturation transition, direction\n      aliases, independent BTB conflicts, jump-to-branch changes, retained\n      history after stale invalidation, disabled/ineligible updates and\n      simultaneous lookup/training old-state semantics.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all architectural assertions; update only predictions\n      dependent on the former tagged-counter policy. Exercise recurrent\n      loops, exits and opposing aliases, BTB eviction and code changes,\n      jumps, illegal/misaligned transfers and imem/load-use/dmem/division\n      holds. Require exact accepted prediction capture, once-only updates,\n      immediate mismatch recovery, correct RVFI PCs/order/traps, bounded\n      progress and absence of wrong-path register or memory effects.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
