a valid advancing EX instruction's resolved next PC differs from its saved prediction, rather than on every taken control transfer. Keep the resolved next PC as the source of RVFI pc_wdata. Correct predictions admit the fetched successor immediately; incorrect taken, not-taken, or target predictions recover using the existing one-bubble redirect path.  Train the indexed counter once per valid legal conditional branch accepted by EX, using its actual tak\n critical: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_2_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -187.641, 'arrival_ns': 197.935, 'logic_cells': 150, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u\n…[23879 of 26951 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dd79430b435108c9]…\n miss, invalid or unrepresentable lookup predicts not taken with zero target. A valid hit exposes its original stored target even when not taken. Fetch lookup remains a function of registered PC and predictor storage; it does not inspect instruction-memory data or compute a target adder.  On each original EX-accepted, legal conditional-branch update with an in-range aligned PC and representable aligned direct target, saturate only the indexed direction counter using actual taken. Apply ordinary saturation to its existing value without consulting target-buffer validity, tag, jump kind or replacement status. Direction aliases intentionally share history. Jump, ordinary, illegal, trapping and disabled updates neither train nor invalidate direction history. BTB eviction, stale invalidation and\n critical: {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_product_65_s1', 'slack_ns': -8.745, 'arrival_ns': 18.85, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_predictor', 'cpu/u_id']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
