ate-versus-invalidate,\nsix-bit index, twelve-bit tag, eighteen-bit target, counter and jump kind.\nTable payload writes and validity updates then use only this saved commit\ncommand on the next edge. A transaction accepted on edge N therefore\nbecomes lookup-visible after edge N+2. Allocation updates every row field\natomically; invalidation clears only validity. A nonallocating tag miss\ncreates no write. Pending stages drain independently of later EX/MEM\nreadiness; there is one transaction per edge and no queue interlock.\n\nForward the pending commit row into maintenance when its index equals\nthe transaction being processed. Allocation forwards valid/tag/counter/\njump; invalidation forwards valid=0. Compare the forwarded tag with the\ntransaction tag before counter reuse. This \n…[7713 of 10785 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8a602091fe3389de]…\nd disabled updates neither\ntrain nor invalidate direction history. BTB eviction, stale invalidation\nand changes between jump and branch likewise leave direction history\nintact. No reset-to-weak mux is driven by a BTB hit comparison.\n\nPreserve the complete original target-buffer policy independently:\naccepted legal representable branches and jumps allocate or overwrite\ntag/target/kind and set validity; a not-taken branch stores its direct\ntarget, never PC+4. Ordinary, illegal, trapping and unrepresentable-target\nupdates invalidate only a matching BTB tag. Other tag misses do nothing.\nRetain every full-PC/full-target upper-bit and alignment check before\ntruncation. Reset clears BTB validity, resets direction counters to 01\nand wins over updates. A first not-taken update moves 01 to 00; this\nintentionally differs from the former weak replacement initialization.\nLookup on a training edge observes old state; do not add write-through\nforwarding or alter the prediction metadata captured by ID/EX\nRAS-related titles:\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
