{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_79", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r15s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-003-r15s2\ntitle: \"Register only direct BTB allocation eligibility before execute\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 194.25 iterations/sec at 81.537 MHz with 4,197,447\n  timed CoreMark cycles. Predictor experiments repeatedly expose paths from\n  branch resolution through predictor maintenance into ID or validity clock\n  enables. The original allocation gate consumes effective EX legality,\n  whose conditional-branch misalignment term depends on the late branch\n  outcome, despite allocation independently rejecting every misaligned\n  target. A local one-bit direction prototype passed retirement cosim and\n  CRC validation but scored only 74.114 MHz in placement option zero; its\n  worst path still ended at predictor validity enable. Changing direction\n  accuracy therefore did not remove the relevant allocation dependency.\n  LESSONS.md is absent.\nhypothesis: |\n  Prepare only the eligibility of direct control-flow allocations at the\n  existing ID/EX boundary. Add one predictor_direct_ok bit to id_ex_t.\n  In ID compute a temporary full-width candidate = fetch PC + decoded\n  immediate. Set the bit exactly when the validated decoder identifies a\n  legal conditional branch or JAL, excluding JALR, and candidate[31:20]\n  is zero and candidate[1:0] is zero. Capture this one bit with its\n  instruction; clear it on reset, flush or bubble and retain it on every\n  existing hold. Do not register the candidate target word or use this\n  temporary sum for architectural execution.\n\n  In EX expose the registered direct-control kind and this captured\n  eligibility bit to branch_predictor alongside the original accepted\n  update transaction. For a direct branch/JAL, use the saved bit as the\n  predictor allocation qualifier instead of recomputing effective legality\n  and representability from live EX resolution. Continue to qualify the\n  update itself with original ex_accept and full update-PC range/alignment.\n  For JALR retain the original effective-legality, jump-kind and full\n  resolved-target range\n…[4251 of 7323 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ad723b9c6216f540]…\nactly intact.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect the two internal predictor preparation signals through EX to\n      the predictor. Preserve top-level IO, hazard controls and RVFI.\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all original policy assertions. Initialize new inputs for\n      legacy resolved-qualifier tests and add direct-prequalified cases.\n      Compare all row transitions with the original predictor under\n      equivalent direct qualifiers, including both branch outcomes,\n      replacements, kind changes, invalid targets and stale invalidation.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve architectural assertions and check eligibility lifetime\n      across load-use, imem/dmem holds, division, flush and reset. Exercise\n      aligned, misaligned and range-boundary direct targets plus JALR\n      fallback. Require exact PCs, links, traps, operands, order, once-only\n      memory effects, wrong-path suppression and forward progress.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
