ndexed counter's MSB is\\nset; predict JAL taken unconditionally. Construct B/J immediates directly\\nfrom the instruction and add them to the current fetch PC. Predict only\\nword-aligned targets; use PC+4 for all other instructions, including JALR,\\nreserved branch encodings, and misaligned direct targets. Do not add a BTB,\\nreturn-address stack, global history, cache, or arithmetic redesign.\\n\\nCarry the exact predicted next PC with each accepted instruction through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX. Advance the PC to that prediction only when the existing\\nfetch/decode handshake accepts the instruction. Prediction must not advance\\nthe PC during imem backpressure, load-use interlocks, or dmem backp\n…[13091 of 16163 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4bdea66183de3ec2]…\nd connect the predictor between registered fetch PC,\\nIF prediction selection and EX acceptance/update feedback. Keep the\\nexact nret=1 IO and RVFI contract and the champion divider handshake.\\nEliminate the redundant EX-redirect-to-IF-instruction-mask feedback.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Include the new predictor source in the runner. Add directed loops\\nand exits, changing and recurring JALR targets, taken/not-taken\\nmistakes, same-index different-tag conflicts, simultaneous lookup/\\nupdate, stale hits after instruction changes, reserved encodings,\\nmisaligned and nonrepresentable targets, and reset with populated\\nentries. Exercise imem/load-use/dmem/division holds around prediction\\nand recovery, including poisoned wrong-path stores and source bits.\\nAssert exact retirement PCs, RVFI next PCs and order, architectural\\nvalues, accepted-store counts, bounded progress, and no duplicate\\nupdates while EX is held. Use an edge-accurate stalled bus model.\\n'}]}\nNotes: \nLessons: False\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
