te decisions must depend exclusively on the registered pending\n  transaction and stored table state. Live EX update inputs may feed\n  only the training registers. Lookup uses the registered fetch PC and\n  committed table contents, with no combinational forwarding from live\n  or\n…[3337 of 6409 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1d41e906a8f65d27]…\n  and commit edges without dropping any policy assertion. Add streams\n      of back-to-back outcomes at one PC, alternating conflicting tags,\n      jump/branch transitions, target overwrites and stale invalidations.\n      Check old lookup state during capture, ordered visible commits,\n      disabled-update bubbles, no live-input or pending-data bypass,\n      exactly-once commit, and reset canceling a pending transaction.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Keep every existing architectural/stall regression and add tight\n      loops and conflicting control-flow PCs exercising delayed training.\n      Exercise accepted training followed by imem/dmem, load-use and\n      division holds, reset with a pending update, and stale instruction\n      replacement. Assert saved prediction recovery, resolved RVFI PCs,\n      monotonic retirement, progress and no wrong-path register/store\n      effects. Do not alter the architectural acceptance or recovery\n      controls to accommodate the training delay.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
