 \"slack_ns\": -8.71,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 19.004,\n      \"logic_cells\": 10,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_id\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r5s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r5s2',\n'title':'Train the predictor from registered EX/MEM control-flow results',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion reaches 170.74 iter/sec with median Fmax 71.668 MHz and\n4197447 stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. Its current predictor trains\ndirectly from combinational EX outcome, target, trap and acceptance logic.\nUpdates therefore fan out from EX into tag, target, direction and validity\nstorage on the same edge that resolves the control transfer. The existing\nEX/MEM bundle already registers the PC, controls, outcome, branch target\nand architectural next PC needed for training.\n\nNo LESSONS.md exists. Prior capacity reduction and target banking did not\nbeat the latest champion. A baseline reproduction passed canonical CRCs,\nbounds and completion with exactly 4197447 bracket cycles. Sequential\nreplay counted only 62551 predictor misses in 2922016 timed retirements;\na small history predictor and return stack removed fewer than 2000 each.\nA constant-row full-tag BTB prototype preserved cycles but placement 1\nreached only 72.212 MHz, below acceptance, with 7424 logic cells and 3841\nregisters. Its timing reports expose long EX-to-predictor update paths.\nRegistered predictor feedback is a distinct way to shorten those paths\nwithout increasing target capacity, adding broad flop tables or relying\non a large accuracy gain. The champion's ALU remains a competing limit.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Move only the predictor-training boundary from combinational EX acceptance\nto consumption of the existing registered EX/MEM instruction in MEM.\nKeep the exact 64-entry direct-mapped predictor, all tag/target/counter\nwidths, PC-only lookup, bimodal direction policy, jump behavior, range and\nalignment guards, and old-row lookup timing. Do not change instruction\npipeline depth, operand forwarding, arithmetic, fetch acceptance or the\nEX misprediction-recovery boundary. This is one predictor feedback-pipeline\nexperiment; no capacity, banking, history or metadata redesign is included.\n\nDrive predictor_update_en from ex_mem_w.valid && \"'!hold_mem_wb && !reset.\nThis consumes one registered instruction exactly once: a true data-memory\nhold suppresses training until MEM accepts, and the existing EX/MEM hold\nor bubble behavior prevents repeats after consumption. Derive update_pc\nfrom ex_mem_w.pc, branch/jump kind from its registered controls and legal\nfrom !ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_illegal. Derive actual taken as legal AND\n(ex_mem_w.branch_taken OR ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_jump). For jumps, update_target\nis ex_mem_w.pc_next, the registered architectural jump destination; for\nconditional branches it is ex_mem_w.branch_target, including the direct\ntarget on a not-taken outcome. Never substitute PC+4 for a not-taken branch\ntraining target. On illegal or misaligned control transfers the registered\ntrap control marks the update illegal, so the unchanged predictor performs\nmatching-only invalidation instead of allocation. Non-control instructions\nstill provide registered stale-entry invalidation opportunities.\n\nRemove the seven combinational predictor_update outputs and assignments\nfrom ex_stage and derive them centrally from EX/MEM in core. Keep the\nexisting branch_taken, branch_target, pc_next, PC and effective controls\nregistered in ex_stage; these fields already contain the required results.\nDo not forward current EX values around this boundary and do not add an\nEX-to-fetch bypass for freshly trained entries. The training transaction\nbecomes visible one edge later than today. A cold or changed target may\ntherefore require another recovery before training catches up; saved\nprediction metadata and independent EX resolution guarantee correctness.\nKeep predictor read-during-write behavior unchanged: lookup before a write\nedge uses old state, and the accepted prediction is retained through holds.\n\nEX continues to resolve direction and full-width target, detect traps and\ncompare the actual outcome against the exact prediction accepted by ID.\nRecovery stays qualified by valid EX acceptance, suppresses held/dividing\ninstructions, overrides fetch stalls and synchronously kills the younger\nbundle. Do not delay recovery together with training. Preserve reset,\nload-use and bus interlocks, finalized held operands, sticky division\ncompletion, true multiplier behavior and ALTOPS substitutions. Preserve\nnret=1 and every RVFI field, consecutive retirement order, decoder default\nlegality, trap handling, memory bounds, canonical CRC validation and\nmarker-bracketed timing. Modify only allowed RTL and cocotb suites.\n\nThe initial expectation is a six-percent fitness gain with low confidence.\nTraining uses existing stage flops, although their previously verification-\nonly PC/target/control fields may now remain in the timed netlist. Shorter\nEX feedback and reduced direct table-write fanout must outweigh that cost,\nany extra cold/conflicting-branch misses and the remaining ALU timing path.\nMeasure actual stalled CoreMark cycles and all three vendor placements;\naccept only a fitness product more than 4.6 percent above 170.74. At unchanged\ncycles that requires approximately 74.965 MHz median Fmax. Full formal,\nretirement cosim, decoder/arithmetic and existing correctness gates remain\nmandatory; no evaluation or benchmark source may change.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Derive all predictor training fields from registered EX/MEM and its\nonce-only MEM consumption enable. Retain existing predictor instantiation,\nlookup, recovery wiring, bus semantics and the nret=1 top-level contract.\nRemove connections to combinational EX training outputs.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Remove only the seven predictor_update output ports and their direct\ncombinational assignments. Preserve immediate accepted-EX redirect logic\nand register the existing PC, effective trap controls, branch_taken,\nbranch_target and architectural pc_next exactly as today for MEM training.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Keep all existing architectural assertions. Add immediate repeated branches,\ncold and conflicting targets, changing JALR targets, stale ordinary hits,\nmisaligned branch/jump traps and back-to-back control transfers under imem\nand dmem stalls and division waits. Check the one-cycle training delay,\nexactly one update per registered instruction consumption, no update during\nMEM holds or reset, unchanged immediate EX recovery, exact RVFI PC/source/\nresult/order and once-only memory effects. Use hierarchical observations\nonly for predictor training timing; architectural assertions stay intact.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_branch_predictor.py','description':'''Retain every existing predictor policy, capacity, output, saturation,\nreplacement, kind-change, invalidation, range/alignment and simultaneous\nlookup/update/reset assertion. Predictor policy itself is unchanged;\nverify registered transactions preserve the same update semantics.\n'''}]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef text_representer(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,text_representer)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Registered-training hypothesis is complete and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
