{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r5s2.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());h['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':2,'confidence':'medium'}\na=h['hypothesis'].index('The initial expectation is a six-percent fitness gain')\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'][:a]+'''An isolated EX/MEM-training prototype passes stalled and zero-wait RVFI\nretirement comparisons for selftest and all three random programs. The\nunchanged canonical stalled CoreMark run completes in bounds, passes all\nCRC/completion/bracketing checks and retains exactly 4197447 bracket cycles\nfor ten iterations. Gowin placement options 0/1/2 measure 68.097, 72.748 and\n72.748 MHz, median 72.748 MHz, with 4715 logic cells, 1956 registers,\n32 LUT-RAM units, five BSRAMs and two DSPs. Estimated fitness is 173.315\niter/sec, approximately 1.51 percent above 170.74. This measured prototype\nis below the required 178.594 acceptance threshold; do not claim a win.\nThe expected integer gain is two percent with medium confidence.\n\nShorter feedback reduces direct EX-to-table coupling, but the ALU remains\nthe worst measured path and limits the overall benefit. Some existing\nEX/MEM fields previously pruned as verification-only are now retained in\nthe timed circuit. Final implementation must still pass unchanged lint,\nformal, arithmetic/decoder tests, retirement cosim and canonical CoreMark\nvalidation, then be scored using the actual median Gowin timing product.\nPreserve every invariant and don't-touch file.\n'''\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef rep(d,v):return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',v,style='|' if '\\\\n' in v else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated hypothesis with measured median timing and explicit sub-threshold result')\nprint('Exact estimated fitness:',72.748e6*10/4197447)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
