{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_65", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r7s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r7s2',\n 'title':'Prepare predictor verification and repair destinations before EX',\n 'category':'predictor',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 canonical stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The existing tagged predictor already leaves only about 62551 misses, so more direction history or target capacity is unlikely to clear the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold. Prior compact-capacity, asynchronous-banking, registered-training and synchronous-lookahead attempts failed to beat the latest champion. Instead shorten the arithmetic feeding predictor verification, training and recovery while retaining its exact policy and one-cycle recovery penalty.\n\nAn isolated prototype that registers only the direct PC-relative target in ID measures 79.190, 83.917 and 83.917 MHz across Gowin placement options 0/1/2, median 83.917 MHz, with 4618 logic cells and 1889 registers. That preliminary 2.9 percent Fmax gain is below acceptance, so the final hypothesis also prepares the sequential recovery/link destination at the same boundary. This is one destination-preparation change; predictor capacity, target encoding and speculation latency remain unchanged.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Compute and register both possible PC-derived destinations at the existing ID/EX acceptance edge: pc_relative_target = in.pc + decoded_imm, and sequential_target = in.pc + 4. Add these two full-width words to id_ex_t. ID already has the source PC and decoded immediate independently of operand forwarding, so these adders run in parallel with register access rather than after the EX launch boundary. Do not add an instruction pipeline stage or an early target-equality comparison through the asynchronous BTB lookup.\n\nIn EX use the registered pc_relative_target for direct conditional-branch targets and JAL targets, for predictor update_target even when the branch resolves not taken, and for the corresponding full-width saved-prediction target comparison. Keep JALR's rs1+imm calculation and bit-zero clearing in EX because it depends on finalized architectural operands. Use sequential_target for architectural PC+4 fallthrough/recovery and for the PC+4 link result of both JAL and JALR. Keep existing branch comparison, legality, alignment traps, direction/target mismatch factoring and EX-accept qualifications. The intended timing gain is removing PC-derived adders from prediction verification/training/recovery and from the link-value path, while avoiding a new BTB-lookup-to-adder-to-target-match path in ID.\n\nRetain exactly the current 64-entry direct-mapped BTB, full tags, absolute 18-bit stored targets, two-bit saturating counters, unconditional-jump behavior, reset-only validity, full range/alignment guards and matching-only stale invalidation. Keep once-per-EX-accept training, old-row read/update behavior, IF PC advancement and every memory/load-use/division interlock. Every new destination word must be captured with its own instruction and PC, remain fixed through ID/EX holds, and clear with the existing reset/flush/bubble behavior. Compute the full 32-bit sum, including alignment and wraparound bits: narrowing or assuming same-region targets would change coverage.\n\nPrediction remains advisory. EX must still resolve the actual branch outcome, changing JALR destinations, illegal instructions, stale ordinary hits and misaligned targets independently, recover immediately when its accepted metadata mismatches, and suppress wrong-path register/store effects. Full-width architectural next PCs, link values and all RVFI fields must remain identical. Preserve nret=1 and exact top-level IO, decoder default-illegal discipline, arithmetic and ALTOPS behavior, sticky division completion, strict RVFI order, memory bounds and all unchanged correctness/fitness gates. Do not change pipeline depth, train from MEM, delay recovery or alter the predictor tables.\n\nEstimate a 7 percent fitness improvement with low confidence until the complete prepared-destination variant is measured. At unchanged 4197447 bracket cycles, median Gowin Fmax must exceed about 85.29 MHz; the direct-only prototype does not establish a win. The main risk is moving the limiting path to ID's PC/immediate adder or increasing routing pressure from the extra flops. Score only actual median vendor Fmax times canonical marker-bracketed iterations/cycle with the contract's random bus stalls.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add full-width pc_relative_target and sequential_target words to id_ex_t only. Keep all predictor metadata, controls, operands, instruction/PC identity, later-stage bundles and retirement width intact.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute PC+decoded immediate and PC+4 in ID and capture both on the existing accepted ID/EX edge. Clear both with reset/flush/bubble and retain them during all holds. Keep decoder legality, operand forwarding and multiplier formatting unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use prepared PC-relative targets for direct branches/JAL and prepared sequential destinations for fallthrough, prediction repair and JAL/JALR link values. Keep operand-dependent JALR addition in EX. Preserve exact predictor update targets, full-width mismatch detection, alignment traps, effective producers, acceptance and immediate recovery.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing architectural assertions and predictor tests. Add directed PC-relative target capture checks across positive/negative immediates, aligned and misaligned targets, JAL versus JALR links, and address-region boundaries. Hold these words through imem, load-use, dmem and division stalls; verify reset/flush discard. Exercise loop exits, stale entries and changed indirect targets, asserting exact RVFI PC continuity/order/link data and no wrong-path memory effects. Require unchanged lint/formal, predictor/decoder/arithmetic tests, eight stalled/zero-wait retirement comparisons and canonical CoreMark CRC/bounds/bracketing validation before actual vendor fitness scoring.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
