[31:16] + in.imm[31:16] + target_carry, discarding overflow exactly as ordinary RV32 modular addition does. Reconstruct the full target as {upper_sum, target_low}. This splits one 32-bit carry dependency into two clock-separated 16-bit portions using only 17 new flops, with no extra instruction latency.\n\nUse this reconstructed destination for conditional branches and JAL, for the full-width saved-prediction target comparison, and for predictor update_target including not-taken branches. Keep JALR's full rs1+imm computation and bit-zero clearing in EX because it depends on finalized operands. Preserve existing PC+4 calculation and JAL/JALR link values. Keep the balanced branch comparator, decoded legality, precise alignment traps, actual-taken definition, direction/target mismatch factoring, EX acceptance and immediate recovery. Do not move target equality into ID: a separately measured early-equality prototype created a long asynchronous-BTB-to-target-check path.\n\nPreserve exactly the existing 64-entry direct-mapped BTB, PC[7:2] index, full tags, absolute 18-bit stored targets, two-bit saturating counters, unconditional jumps, old-row lookup/update behavior, range/alignment guards, reset-only validity and matching-only stale invalidation. Keep training once per accepted EX instruction, full-width actual targets and current speculation/recovery latency. No target-region restriction, capacity reduction, MEM training, synchronous lookahead or predictor policy change is included.\n\nCapture low sum and carry only on the same existing ID/EX edge as their PC/immediate/instruction. Hold them through data-memory stalls, load-use interlocks and division waits; clear them with the existing reset, flush and bubble assignment. Carry must come from unsigned addition of the two low halves even for a negative sign-extended immediate. The upper sum uses that immediate's existing upper bits, preserving negative offsets, 16-bit boundary crossings, alignment bits and 32-bit wraparound exactly. Do not infer an unsigned branch-immediate interpretation or truncate the full target before its architectural/predictor guards.\n\nPrediction remains advisory. EX independently resolves branches, JALR, stale ordinary hits, illegal instructions and misalignment, recovers immediately on accepted mismatch, and suppresses wrong-path register/store effects. Preserve nret=1, exact top-level IO, full-width resolved RVFI PCs and link results, strict retirement order, decoder defaults, arithmetic/ALTOPS and sticky division semantics, memory bounds, canonical CRCs and all unchanged verification/eval gates. Modify only the listed allowed RTL/test paths.\n\nEstimate a 6 percent fitness gain with low confidence until the split-adder implementation is measured. The full-target-register prototype is below acceptance; its result supports the timing direction but is not a measurement of this split variant. With unchanged 4197447 bracket cycles, median Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 85.29 MHz. Main risks are the remaining 16-bit EX target adder, the new ID low-half path, synthesis restructuring and competing ALU/forwarding paths. Score only actual median vendor Fmax times canonical marker-bracketed iterations/cycle under the existing bus stalls.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add a 16-bit target_low and one-bit target_carry to id_ex_t. Retain the full PC and sign-extended immediate, unchanged prediction metadata, execution controls/operands, later-stage payloads and retirement width.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute the zero-extended 17-bit low-half PC+decoded-immediate sum and capture its result/carry on the existing accepted ID/EX edge. Reset/flush/bubble clear both; all holds retain them. Preserve decoder legality, operand forwarding and multiplier formatting.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Complete PC-relative target addition with a 16-bit upper sum using the registered PC/immediate upper halves and saved carry. Use the reconstructed full target for branches/JAL, prediction target verification, actual recovery and predictor training including not-taken branches. Leave JALR arithmetic, PC+4/link computation, branch comparison, trap behavior, producers, acceptance and immediate recovery intact.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing architectural and predictor assertions. Add direct-target arithmetic cases around low-half carry/no-carry, negative branch/JAL offsets, 0xffff/0x10000 boundaries, full-width wraparound, aligned/misaligned targets and changing JALR targets. Hold low sum/carry through imem, load-use, dmem and division stalls and verify reset/flush discard. Check exact RVFI PCs/order/link data, once-only training and absence of wrong-path stores. Require unchanged lint/formal, predictor/decoder/arithmetic tests, eight stalled/zero-wait retirement comparisons and canonical CoreMark CRC/bounds/bracketing validation before actual median vendor fitness scoring.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Split-target hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Split-target hypothesis validates: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r7s2.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
