{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_80", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r7s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Register direct predictor verification targets before EX'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 canonical stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The existing 64-entry tagged predictor leaves only about 62551 misses, so more target capacity, history or return prediction offers too little cycle gain to clear the 4.6 percent threshold. Relevant history includes the successful original tagged predictor, the accuracy loss from compact capacity, and unsuccessful full-width target banking, MEM training and synchronous lookahead. The most promising remaining predictor angle is moving direct-target arithmetic ahead of EX's prediction verification, training and repair feedback while preserving the exact prediction policy and recovery latency.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Compute the full 32-bit direct PC-relative destination in ID, in parallel with operand access, and register it at the existing ID/EX acceptance boundary as pc_relative_target = in.pc + decoded_imm. Add only that one word to id_ex_t. Retain the original PC and sign-extended immediate because other instruction paths and RVFI still use them. Do not add a pipeline stage or compute a predictor target-equality bit through the asynchronous BTB lookup in ID.\n\nIn EX replace its PC+immediate direct-target calculation with the accepted instruction's registered pc_relative_target. Use that destination for conditional branches and JAL, full-width saved-prediction target verification, predictor update_target even on a not-taken branch, and the corresponding architectural redirect destination. Keep JALR's full rs1+imm calculation and bit-zero clearing in EX, as it depends on finalized architectural operands. Keep PC+4 fallthrough and JAL/JALR link computation unchanged. The intended timing gain is removing the direct-target carry chain from EX's predictor verification/training/recovery cone; destination formation in ID runs independently of forwarded branch operands.\n\nPreserve exactly the current 64-entry direct-mapped BTB, full tags and absolute stored targets, two-bit saturating counters, unconditional-jump behavior, PC-only asynchronous lookup, reset-only validity, full range/alignment guards, weak replacement initialization and matching-only stale invalidation. Retain the balanced branch comparator, actual direction resolution, target mismatch factoring, traps and immediate EX-accept-qualified recovery. Keep once-per-EX-accept training and old-row lookup/update semantics. No target restriction, capacity reduction, banking, history change, registered recovery, MEM training, sequential-destination preparation or split target adder is included.\n\nThe new word must be captured with its source PC, immediate and instruction on precisely the existing ID/EX acceptance edge, retained through every ID/EX hold, and cleared by the existing reset/flush/bubble assignment. Compute a full-width modular sum so positive/negative immediates, address-boundary crossings, wraparound and both alignment bits are preserved. Predictor state remains advisory: EX must independently resolve changing JALR destinations, stale ordinary hits, illegal instructions and misaligned transfers, recover on accepted mismatch and suppress wrong-path register/store effects. Preserve nret=1 and exact top-level IO, full-width architectural/RVFI PCs and links, strict retirement order, decoder defaults, arithmetic/ALTOPS and sticky division semantics, memory bounds, canonical CRCs and all unchanged correctness/fitness gates. Modify only the listed allowed RTL and tests.\n\nAn isolated implementation passed strict Verilator cosim builds, eight full retirement comparisons (selftest and three random programs, each zero-wait and stalled), and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/completion/bounds/bracketing validation at exactly 4197447 timed cycles. All 34 existing pipeline cocotb cases also passed. Gowin placement options 0/1/2 measured 79.190, 83.917 and 83.917 MHz, median 83.917 MHz, with 4618 logic cells, 1889 registers, 32 LUT-RAM units, five BSRAMs and two DSPs. Median Fmax times iterations/cycle yields approximately 199.924 iter/sec, 2.92 percent above 194.25. This is below the required 203.186 iter/sec acceptance score; do not claim a champion win. Expected integer improvement is 3 percent with medium confidence in this measured prototype. Final implementation still requires the unchanged formal gate and fresh vendor/CoreMark scoring.\n\nExperiments with early target-equality capture, sequential-target preparation and a split direct-target adder produced worse timing; keep this hypothesis to the measured full direct-target registration. The residual worst paths pass through ALU/operand forwarding, which limits gains from predictor feedback alone. At unchanged cycle count, median Fmax must exceed about 85.29 MHz to clear acceptance. Score only actual median vendor timing times canonical marker-bracketed iterations/cycle with the existing random bus stalls.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':3,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add one full-width pc_relative_target word to id_ex_t. Retain full PC/immediate, original predictor metadata, execution controls/operands, later-stage payloads and nret=1.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute PC+decoded sign-extended immediate in ID and register the full target on the existing accepted ID/EX edge. Hold it with the instruction through every stall and clear it on reset/flush/bubble. Preserve decoding, operand forwarding and multiplier formatting.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use the saved PC-relative destination for branches/JAL, full-width prediction target verification, predictor training targets including not-taken branches, and architectural direct redirects. Keep JALR addition, PC+4/link logic, branch comparison, legality/alignment traps, producer enables, EX acceptance and immediate recovery unchanged.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing architectural/predictor assertions and 34 regression cases. Add directed target-capture coverage for positive/negative branch/JAL immediates, carries across 16-bit boundaries, full-width wraparound and aligned/misaligned destinations. Verify target/instruction pairing under imem, load-use, dmem and division holds, reset and flush. Retain changing JALR, stale-code, wrong-path-store, exact RVFI PC/order/link and once-only training checks. Require unchanged lint/formal, predictor/decoder/arithmetic tests, eight stalled/zero-wait retirement comparisons and canonical CoreMark CRC/bounds/bracketing validation before fresh median Gowin fitness scoring.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261005-003-r7s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Final hypothesis schema validation passed:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
