{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_64", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r8s2',\n'title':'Prediction-and-strength encoding shortens direction-counter training',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior capacity reduction, target banking, delayed training, synchronous lookahead and early direct-target registration did not clear the acceptance threshold. Accuracy headroom is small, and timing repeatedly crosses EX and the predictor. An isolated outcome-independent training prototype exposed four serial next-counter LUTs on a branch-to-ID operand-capture path and measured only 77.301 MHz. Simplifying the two-bit predictor state machine can remove that feedback depth while retaining every prediction and the existing EX training edge.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Re-encode only the existing 64 two-bit conditional direction counters. Let bit 1 remain the taken prediction and bit 0 mean strength: strongly not taken = 01, weakly not taken = 00, weakly taken = 10, strongly taken = 11. This is an isomorphic encoding of the current saturating machine, not a new direction policy. For a matching conditional entry compute next_prediction = strength ? prediction : update_taken and next_strength = (prediction == update_taken). For replacement or jump-to-branch change initialize {update_taken, 1'b0}; jumps retain their unconditional direction bit and may store constant 10 as today. Replace numerical saturation tests and +/- operations entirely with these direct Boolean equations.\n\nKeep the same two-bit asynchronous array, index PC[7:2], validity, tags, target words, jump-kind array, update-hit condition, write port and enable. Counter bit 1 still feeds prediction, so fetch and saved metadata require no change. Preserve matching-only invalidation and all existing eligibility/range/alignment checks. Reset only the valid bitmap, leave payload unreset, and retain old-row lookup before a simultaneous update edge. No table capacity/banking change, untagged direction table, training delay, target retiming, added pipeline stage or altered recovery policy is included.\n\nThe state mapping is exact for both outcomes in all four states: 01 goes to 01/00 for not-taken/taken; 00 goes to 01/10; 10 goes to 00/11; 11 goes to 10/11. Weak replacement initialization and jump-to-conditional reinitialization must use the new encoding; leaving the old not-taken constant 01 would accidentally create a strong state. Lookup must continue to use the prediction bit, not strength. Preserve all accepted-update gating during reset, bubbles, dmem holds and division waits, saved metadata holds/flushes, architectural traps, full-width target verification, immediate EX recovery, stale-code repair and wrong-path side-effect suppression.\n\nEstimate an 8 percent fitness gain with low confidence from removing the feedback arithmetic and saturation-selection levels, at exactly unchanged CoreMark cycles and accuracy. This estimate has not yet been established by vendor timing. Remaining target-guard and ALU-forwarding paths may limit the gain. Require exact cycle equivalence in canonical stalled CoreMark, all CRC/completion/bounds/bracketing checks, unchanged architectural/formal/cosim gates and fresh median Gowin timing. At unchanged cycles, median Fmax must exceed about 85.29 MHz and fitness must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec to clear 4.6 percent acceptance. Preserve nret=1, top-level IO, every hard invariant and all don't-touch paths.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/branch_predictor.sv','description':'''Change only counter encoding, replacement initialization and conditional next-state equations to prediction/strength form. Remove numerical saturation comparisons and increment/decrement expressions. Keep prediction in bit 1, jump initialization 10, the existing update-hit/kind qualification and every tag/target/valid/lookup/write-enable rule unchanged. Preserve inferred asynchronous payload memories and the current EX update edge.'''} ,\n {'file':'test/test_branch_predictor.py','description':'''Preserve every existing policy assertion. Add an exhaustive transition-equivalence check against a conventional two-bit saturating reference for all four states and both outcomes, then seeded longer traces spanning cold allocation, both saturation endpoints, index/tag replacement and jump-to-branch change. Compare visible predictions and targets, not assumptions about the old internal binary encoding. Retain stale invalidation, alignment/range, reset, disabled-update and old-row collision checks.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Keep all existing architectural and recovery-count assertions unchanged. Exercise loop warmup/exit/reentry and alternating outcomes under fetch/load-use/dmem/division holds, stale ordinary or illegal code and changing indirect targets. Require exact RVFI PC/order/source/link behavior and once-only side effects, plus unchanged formal, eight retirement cosim runs and canonical stalled CoreMark cycles/validation before median vendor fitness scoring.'''}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated schema-valid hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
