{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_86", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r8s2',\n'title':'Prevalidate direct predictor maintenance at the ID/EX boundary',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 194.25 iter/sec at 81.537 MHz and 4197447 canonical stalled CoreMark bracket cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior predictor capacity, banking, MEM-training and synchronous-lookahead attempts did not clear acceptance. Registering the full direct target before EX reached 83.917 MHz, a 2.92 percent gain, but left range/alignment and outcome-dependent trap logic in predictor allocation. The strongest remaining angle is to prepare the complete direct target-maintenance transaction, including eligibility, before EX; the predictor's target/tag/valid write control then avoids both the direct-target carry chain and branch-outcome-dependent trap cone.''',\n'hypothesis':'''At the existing ID/EX acceptance boundary register a full 32-bit pc_relative_target = fetch_PC + decoded sign-extended immediate and one predictor_direct_ok bit. Form that bit in ID from validated decoded legality, direct control-flow kind (conditional branch or JAL, excluding JALR), the full target's upper twelve bits being zero, and both alignment bits being zero. Compute target and eligibility together before truncation. This is one early preparation of direct predictor maintenance; it adds no instruction stage or recovery cycle.\n\nIn EX use the saved full direct target for branches and JAL, architectural direct redirects, saved-prediction target verification and predictor update_target, including the destination of a not-taken branch. Retain JALR's full finalized rs1+imm calculation and bit-zero clearing in EX, PC+4/link computation, balanced branch comparison, full-width mismatch checks and architectural trap/next-PC behavior. Capture and hold the target and eligibility with precisely the existing accepted instruction, and clear them with reset/flush/bubbles.\n\nAdd predictor update_direct and update_direct_allocatable inputs. In core derive update_direct from the registered \"'!is_jalr control and update_direct_allocatable from the saved predictor_direct_ok. For an accepted update whose PC is representable, direct allocation uses that saved bit alone; the indirect path retains the current effective legality, jump kind, full target range and alignment checks. Direct false eligibility performs the current matching-only invalidation. Target, tag, jump kind and validity writes for a direct instruction must not depend on actual_taken, branch_cond, effective branch-trap legality or a fresh EX range/alignment reduction. Direction-counter training alone uses the resolved taken outcome. Keep all current two-bit counter encoding, saturation, weak replacement and jump-to-branch rules unchanged.\n\nThe allocation policy is equivalent: decoded illegal and ordinary instructions have a false prepared bit; an aligned in-range branch/JAL allocates; an unrepresentable or misaligned direct target invalidates its own hit regardless of branch outcome, exactly as the existing predictor target guard already requires. Architectural legality remains independent: a not-taken misaligned branch remains legal, while a taken one traps. Preserve the original effective predictor_update_legal and actual predictor_update_taken monitor signals and all existing trap assertions; feed the new eligibility path separately. All decisions remain qualified by the existing once-per-valid EX acceptance, reset, dmem hold and division-wait controls.\n\nKeep the exact 64-entry PC-only asynchronous tagged BTB, original tags/absolute targets, jump behavior, reset-only validity, unreset payload memories and old-row lookup/update semantics. Preserve exact fetched prediction metadata, immediate EX recovery and its stall priority, stale-code and changing-JALR repair, wrong-path side-effect suppression, nret=1 and top-level IO, RVFI/order/PC/link behavior, decoder defaults, true arithmetic/ALTOPS, memory handshakes, all hard invariants and every don'\"'t-touch path. Do not combine counter re-encoding, smaller tables, banked memories, delayed target training or synchronous prediction with this candidate.\n\nEstimate a 6 percent fitness improvement with low confidence. Early full-target registration alone was measured below acceptance; this additional prevalidated allocation bit is a new extension of the same predictor-feedback preparation and is not a demonstrated win. Other isolated maintenance splits and counter rewrites in this investigation timed worse and are excluded. Expect identical canonical CoreMark prediction policy and bracket cycles, but require actual unchanged correctness gates, full CRC/completion/bounds/bracketing validation and fresh median Gowin timing. At 4197447 cycles, median Fmax must exceed about 85.29 MHz and fitness must exceed 203.1855 iter/sec to clear the 4.6 percent margin. The principal risks are the longer ID preparation path, residual JALR allocation and general ALU forwarding.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add full-width pc_relative_target and predictor_direct_ok to id_ex_t only. Keep the original PC/immediate, prediction metadata, operands, controls, later-stage bundles and nret=1 unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute full modular PC+decoded immediate and validated direct-control eligibility including full upper-bit and alignment guards. Capture both fields with the existing ID/EX accepted instruction, hold them through every interlock and clear on existing reset/flush/bubble rules. Preserve decoding, forwarding and multiplier operand preparation.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use the registered full direct target for branches/JAL, independent prediction verification, direct architectural redirects and training destinations, including not-taken branches. Preserve JALR addition, PC+4/link data, traps, actual outcomes, effective legality monitor outputs, EX acceptance, arithmetic and immediate recovery. Handle the predictor-only eligibility field as unused locally when core wires it directly.'},\n {'file':'rtl/branch_predictor.sv','description':'Accept direct-kind and prevalidated direct-allocation metadata. Select direct allocation from the registered flag and retain existing guarded indirect allocation; retain matching-only invalidation otherwise. Keep original counter state machine, storage dimensions, asynchronous lookup, write edge, reset and all prediction/update policies. Prevent branch outcome and fresh direct-target guards from feeding direct tag/target/jump/valid write enables.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Connect the new predictor inputs directly from the accepted ID/EX registered kind and eligibility. Keep EX acceptance and original legality/outcome/target feedback, all top-level ports, hazard controls, retirement and memory wiring intact.'},\n {'file':'test/test_branch_predictor.py','description':'Retain existing policy assertions and supply new direct eligibility inputs in the standalone driver. Compare direct and indirect maintenance against the original allocation/invalidation reference, including ordinary/illegal stale hits, matching/tag-miss replacements, both branch outcomes, all target guards, kind changes, saturation, reset, disabled writes and old-row lookup collisions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve every existing architectural, effective training-legality and recovery-count assertion. Add direct eligibility/target pairing checks across stalls and flushes, full-width positive/negative offsets and boundary crossings, aligned/misaligned taken/not-taken branches, JAL, changing JALR and stale code. Require unchanged formal, all existing unit tests, eight retirement cosim runs and exact canonical stalled CoreMark cycles/validation before median vendor fitness scoring.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
