{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The history shows that recent predictor timing changes stayed below the acceptance margin. I’m investigating return prediction next: the current BTB stores one target per JALR, so a function called from several sites can repeatedly mispredict its return. A small return-address stack could improve accuracy with modest hardware cost."}}
